1
00:04:01,846 --> 00:04:03,885
Stand up.

2
00:04:15,326 --> 00:04:18,845
We defeated you.

3
00:04:19,565 --> 00:04:22,805
A dozen Alps just became martyrs.

4
00:04:23,406 --> 00:04:25,965
You all died, Alps.

5
00:04:37,326 --> 00:04:41,805
Why didn't you check the Alps lost behind you?

6
00:04:41,846 --> 00:04:44,925
Why didn't you inform your brothers?

7
00:04:45,566 --> 00:04:51,805
If you had been careful, even if
four brothers became martyrs...

8
00:04:52,086 --> 00:04:57,965
...you should have exposed the
ambush. But you didn't care and kept going.

9
00:04:58,006 --> 00:04:59,725
You ran away.

10
00:05:01,886 --> 00:05:04,685
But I will teach all of you.

11
00:05:05,286 --> 00:05:07,085
All of you.

12
00:05:11,246 --> 00:05:13,645
Either the easy way..

13
00:05:14,566 --> 00:05:16,845
...or the hard way.

14
00:05:18,006 --> 00:05:18,965
Now..

15
00:05:21,686 --> 00:05:24,085
...I expect all of you in my tent tonight.

16
00:05:34,126 --> 00:05:36,645
You are in trouble, Alps.

17
00:05:38,166 --> 00:05:40,805
Turgut Ghazi will make you pay for this.

18
00:05:45,006 --> 00:05:49,205
Let's go to the tent, come on.

19
00:06:31,366 --> 00:06:34,245
Thinner, sister, thinner.

20
00:06:36,686 --> 00:06:38,365
Praise be.

21
00:06:45,126 --> 00:06:46,285
Ghazi!

22
00:06:46,286 --> 00:06:48,155
May the flood take you, Ghazi!

23
00:06:51,536 --> 00:06:53,855
Help me stay patient, God.

24
00:06:57,086 --> 00:06:58,525
Ulgen.

25
00:06:58,526 --> 00:07:00,645
What happened to you?

26
00:07:00,686 --> 00:07:04,405
Don't even ask, my Bala.

27
00:07:05,726 --> 00:07:07,445
I cannot think clearly.

28
00:07:07,446 --> 00:07:09,805
This Ghazi, may he suffer.

29
00:07:09,806 --> 00:07:15,205
While chasing him to
catch him, I fell down the hill.

30
00:07:15,206 --> 00:07:17,565
Let me see

31
00:07:17,886 --> 00:07:20,245
Get well soon. Come, come, sit and rest.

32
00:07:20,246 --> 00:07:22,525
I can't rest. Who will cook the food?

33
00:07:22,526 --> 00:07:25,685
Come, sit and rest. Or you'll faint.

34
00:07:25,686 --> 00:07:27,205
You'll faint. Hold her.

35
00:07:27,206 --> 00:07:29,205
Careful.

36
00:07:30,086 --> 00:07:31,765
Mother!

37
00:07:32,286 --> 00:07:33,565
Mother!

38
00:07:33,566 --> 00:07:34,125
Mother..

39
00:07:34,126 --> 00:07:35,125
My daughter.

40
00:07:35,126 --> 00:07:36,805
What happened?

41
00:07:38,326 --> 00:07:41,405
Mother, among the sisters,
no one fights better than me.

42
00:07:41,406 --> 00:07:44,405
But my sister didn't let
me rest even for a minute.

43
00:07:45,326 --> 00:07:47,925
You are right about your fighting skills.

44
00:07:47,926 --> 00:07:51,485
But you must keep
training until you fight like us.

45
00:07:53,846 --> 00:07:56,645
Stop training now.

46
00:07:59,326 --> 00:08:02,165
I will give you a duty.

47
00:08:02,886 --> 00:08:05,685
Mother... What duty is it?

48
00:08:05,686 --> 00:08:08,965
You will cook dinner tonight.

49
00:08:08,966 --> 00:08:11,885
You will prepare your father's table.

50
00:08:11,886 --> 00:08:13,565
Us?

51
00:08:13,846 --> 00:08:16,445
But mother, I'm still learning.

52
00:08:18,166 --> 00:08:19,805
Mother..

53
00:08:20,606 --> 00:08:22,125
Are you sure?

54
00:08:22,126 --> 00:08:24,045
Or else we might starve.

55
00:08:24,046 --> 00:08:25,725
Aunt..

56
00:08:25,966 --> 00:08:27,325
Why would you say that?

57
00:08:27,326 --> 00:08:29,645
No my Fatma, I'm joking.

58
00:08:29,646 --> 00:08:31,245
But I'll help them, mother.

59
00:08:31,246 --> 00:08:33,525
No, no.

60
00:08:34,126 --> 00:08:36,965
Only the two of them will do it. You can do it.

61
00:08:39,885 --> 00:08:41,885
Are they going to compete?

62
00:08:41,885 --> 00:08:45,285
Whose food is better, Bala Hatun?

63
00:08:46,286 --> 00:08:48,365
Don't grow the fire!

64
00:08:49,046 --> 00:08:52,285
I can't even get up. They are already nervous!

65
00:08:52,806 --> 00:08:56,205
Ulgen. Calm down.

66
00:08:57,566 --> 00:08:59,205
Ghazi..

67
00:09:01,406 --> 00:09:04,285
You can do it, girls, you can. Go now.

68
00:09:04,446 --> 00:09:08,685
We can. We can, mother but where is my father?

69
00:09:08,686 --> 00:09:10,725
Let's ask him what he wants to eat.

70
00:09:10,726 --> 00:09:12,765
Your father is not in the tribe, my daughter.

71
00:09:12,766 --> 00:09:15,365
He'll see you when he comes in the evening.

72
00:09:15,646 --> 00:09:18,285
Mother, where is my father?

73
00:09:18,286 --> 00:09:20,365
I don't know, my daughter.

74
00:09:21,526 --> 00:09:23,125
Come on.

75
00:09:24,406 --> 00:09:27,045
I will make the best food for my father.

76
00:09:27,526 --> 00:09:30,925
Don't even run. We'll start at the same time.

77
00:09:30,926 --> 00:09:33,685
Halime, I told you to stop.

78
00:10:25,086 --> 00:10:28,205
O passenger! Where are you going?

79
00:10:28,206 --> 00:10:29,645
To The Red Apple.

80
00:10:29,646 --> 00:10:31,205
What is your goal?

81
00:10:31,206 --> 00:10:32,485
Shahada.

82
00:10:32,486 --> 00:10:34,485
What do you want to reunite with?

83
00:10:34,646 --> 00:10:35,885
With the state.

84
00:10:35,886 --> 00:10:37,485
Where is the state?

85
00:10:37,766 --> 00:10:40,165
The whole world.

86
00:10:43,286 --> 00:10:45,045
O, the one waiting.

87
00:10:45,046 --> 00:10:51,485
For the sake of armies whose horses spark
fire and whose swords bring justice, tell me.

88
00:10:52,846 --> 00:10:54,325
Where is the Red Apple?

89
00:11:40,846 --> 00:11:43,125
-Peace be upon you.
-Peace be upon you too.

90
00:11:44,446 --> 00:11:45,885
Have a seat, Osman Bey.

91
00:11:46,686 --> 00:11:47,805
Thank you.

92
00:11:56,366 --> 00:11:58,765
Osman Bey, son of Ertugrul Ghazi.

93
00:11:59,646 --> 00:12:02,685
You didn't disappoint

94
00:12:03,326 --> 00:12:05,285
You brought Mongolians to kneel.

95
00:12:05,646 --> 00:12:07,605
You devastated Byzantine.

96
00:12:08,366 --> 00:12:10,525
You became victorious in both fronts.

97
00:12:10,646 --> 00:12:12,045
Thank you, thank you.

98
00:12:13,606 --> 00:12:17,525
We didn't get victorious thanks
to our strength but our faith.

99
00:12:18,246 --> 00:12:21,205
I'm trying to spread Islam, the right religion.

100
00:12:21,406 --> 00:12:24,445
And I will never give up.

101
00:12:24,926 --> 00:12:26,445
Surely, Osman Bey.

102
00:12:26,846 --> 00:12:31,245
We heard, saw and confirmed.

103
00:12:32,886 --> 00:12:39,045
But you should know that there
are harder times ahead of you.

104
00:12:39,606 --> 00:12:42,845
You fate is between a scorpion's clamps.

105
00:12:46,086 --> 00:12:48,725
The enemy got defeated but...

106
00:12:49,326 --> 00:12:51,045
...they are gaining power again.

107
00:12:51,606 --> 00:12:53,925
They'll attack you with all their strength.

108
00:12:55,686 --> 00:13:00,005
It won't be a war of welfare.

109
00:13:01,246 --> 00:13:03,765
But it's a war of existence.

110
00:13:06,006 --> 00:13:08,845
I'm trying to make the state prevail forever.

111
00:13:10,086 --> 00:13:14,005
We are never afraid of death.

112
00:13:14,846 --> 00:13:17,005
I don't care if they all attack.

113
00:13:22,326 --> 00:13:27,045
But you are getting weaker
in this fight day by day.

114
00:13:28,406 --> 00:13:31,805
Your struggle has caused great wounds in you.

115
00:13:32,686 --> 00:13:35,845
The number of your alps has decreased.

116
00:13:38,006 --> 00:13:40,445
I know. I know.

117
00:13:41,366 --> 00:13:43,005
You say you know, Osman Bey.

118
00:13:43,086 --> 00:13:46,485
So tell us about the measures you will take.

119
00:13:54,126 --> 00:13:57,525
Alps who cannot use swords are chained.

120
00:13:59,126 --> 00:14:03,005
Alps without a family
jeopardize the future of the state.

121
00:14:04,686 --> 00:14:05,765
For this reason,

122
00:14:06,806 --> 00:14:09,805
...I will make all the single alps get married.

123
00:14:10,926 --> 00:14:13,165
I'll build a commission about that.

124
00:14:13,166 --> 00:14:16,805
I will use every means available.

125
00:14:19,286 --> 00:14:25,565
And the children to be born
will flourish our state forever.

126
00:14:26,566 --> 00:14:28,525
Thank you, Osman bey.

127
00:14:28,926 --> 00:14:31,765
As the number of heathens increases,

128
00:14:32,086 --> 00:14:36,045
...you have do that to be equal to them.

129
00:14:39,126 --> 00:14:43,325
The state is the one that
always foresees the future.

130
00:14:45,846 --> 00:14:49,765
Being minority means annihilation for a nation.

131
00:14:50,606 --> 00:14:53,725
New generations mean hope.

132
00:14:54,886 --> 00:14:56,565
Otherwise

133
00:14:57,486 --> 00:15:01,805
...there will be no liberty in these lands.

134
00:15:03,326 --> 00:15:06,085
We will help you with this.

135
00:15:06,846 --> 00:15:12,885
Turkmen tribes have already left from Iraq
and Aleppo to increase your population.

136
00:15:15,046 --> 00:15:17,125
You will help them settle.

137
00:15:17,846 --> 00:15:23,165
Alps will come to use swords
and merchants to make trade.

138
00:15:24,726 --> 00:15:30,125
In this way, the taxes you
get with both battle and trade...

139
00:15:30,646 --> 00:15:32,565
..will improve your state.

140
00:15:36,166 --> 00:15:41,005
Tax is the most important system
that improves a state, Osman Bey.

141
00:15:41,526 --> 00:15:43,645
It's the insurance of the future.

142
00:15:44,086 --> 00:15:47,405
Of course... Of course, you're right.

143
00:15:50,206 --> 00:15:52,565
We always have place for Turkmen.

144
00:15:53,006 --> 00:15:54,685
They are welcome here.

145
00:15:55,886 --> 00:15:59,565
It'll be better for me if I know when they come.

146
00:16:00,366 --> 00:16:03,365
They will be here in fifteen dawns.

147
00:16:04,206 --> 00:16:10,365
Make them settle in the lands that
you will conquer next, Osman Bey.

148
00:16:11,286 --> 00:16:12,725
Okay.

149
00:16:13,366 --> 00:16:16,485
We herald conquests for you.

150
00:16:17,606 --> 00:16:19,605
May swords be drawn.

151
00:16:20,686 --> 00:16:23,405
May the banner of justice raise in the sky.

152
00:16:24,246 --> 00:16:25,285
Sure.

153
00:16:25,726 --> 00:16:28,325
When the Seljuk State collapsed

154
00:16:28,886 --> 00:16:31,565
...Beys without a head
turned against each other.

155
00:16:32,166 --> 00:16:35,525
While Turks needed to stand united,

156
00:16:35,606 --> 00:16:38,245
...each of them wanted to be the leader.

157
00:16:39,126 --> 00:16:41,565
And they worked for their own.

158
00:16:42,486 --> 00:16:43,565
Of course.

159
00:16:43,886 --> 00:16:50,445
But you, Osman Bey, chose
the Islam cause for Turks.

160
00:16:52,486 --> 00:16:56,085
-You fought the heathens on your own.
-Sure I did.

161
00:16:56,966 --> 00:16:58,245
For this reason

162
00:16:58,566 --> 00:17:00,605
...light the fire of conquest.

163
00:17:03,526 --> 00:17:05,845
It is such a huge fire...

164
00:17:06,806 --> 00:17:11,325
...it will be an ember for the
tyrants and hope for the oppressed.

165
00:17:12,246 --> 00:17:13,285
God willing.

166
00:17:13,526 --> 00:17:18,845
Horses of Turks will reach the
frontiers like the head of a mare!

167
00:17:22,006 --> 00:17:23,805
March, Osman Bey.

168
00:17:24,964 --> 00:17:29,165
You march so the blind dagger
of betrayal will get broken...

169
00:17:31,126 --> 00:17:34,685
...and the justice of Islam will
spread all around the world.

170
00:17:59,446 --> 00:18:01,805
The fire of heathens will go out.

171
00:18:02,886 --> 00:18:05,165
Heathens will be destroyed.

172
00:18:06,126 --> 00:18:07,605
I swear..

173
00:18:07,806 --> 00:18:10,765
...the lands of Turks will flourish.

174
00:18:12,206 --> 00:18:14,125
Either a leader rules...

175
00:18:15,726 --> 00:18:17,725
..or ravens chew dead bodies.

176
00:18:18,086 --> 00:18:19,685
May you live long.

177
00:18:30,446 --> 00:18:34,846
I brought greetings from
Osman Bey, Bey of Beys,

178
00:18:34,858 --> 00:18:39,365
who brought order and
justice in the frontiers.

179
00:18:39,486 --> 00:18:41,805
-Peace be upon you too.
-Peace be upon you too.

180
00:18:42,046 --> 00:18:44,445
Osman Bey is having a council tomorrow.

181
00:18:44,766 --> 00:18:48,845
He desires to see you and all
the other Beys in the council.

182
00:18:48,886 --> 00:18:56,045
We appreciate the regards and
invitation of the heir of Oghuz kin.

183
00:18:56,246 --> 00:19:00,085
But why is Osman Bey having a council?

184
00:19:00,246 --> 00:19:02,725
Do you have any information, Aykurt Cavus.

185
00:19:02,806 --> 00:19:04,445
I don't know, Koca Bey.

186
00:19:04,566 --> 00:19:08,125
My Bey just ordered us to invite the Beys.

187
00:19:08,646 --> 00:19:10,925
As Osman Bey orders.

188
00:19:11,846 --> 00:19:13,045
Okay.

189
00:19:19,446 --> 00:19:22,405
Osman Bey is expecting all his Beys tomorrow.

190
00:19:22,566 --> 00:19:23,685
He'II hold a council.

191
00:19:23,806 --> 00:19:26,125
He orders you to join, Hasan Bey.

192
00:19:26,246 --> 00:19:29,245
Osman Bey, the conquer.

193
00:19:29,446 --> 00:19:31,045
He's invited all the beys.

194
00:19:31,046 --> 00:19:33,645
It must be an important matter, huh, Kanyumaz?

195
00:19:33,646 --> 00:19:35,445
Kanyumaz doesn't know, Hasan Bey.

196
00:19:35,526 --> 00:19:37,165
I just deliver the message.

197
00:19:37,286 --> 00:19:41,125
When the council starts
tomorrow everyone will know.

198
00:19:41,446 --> 00:19:42,885
Alright, Kanyumaz.

199
00:19:43,446 --> 00:19:45,965
Osman Bey's wish is a command to me.

200
00:19:46,406 --> 00:19:47,565
Sure, my Bey.

201
00:19:50,086 --> 00:19:53,565
Why do you think he's having
a council so suddenly, brother?

202
00:19:53,606 --> 00:19:55,565
We will see when we go.

203
00:19:57,046 --> 00:20:00,445
Did you really not know he would have a council?

204
00:20:00,606 --> 00:20:03,325
Would I have asked if I had known?

205
00:20:04,046 --> 00:20:09,445
As he is gathering all the
beys, it must be an urgent matter.

206
00:20:10,326 --> 00:20:16,245
Obviously, Osman Bey is about
to make an important decision.

207
00:20:17,966 --> 00:20:19,845
And that means...

208
00:20:24,686 --> 00:20:26,325
Excuse me, brother.

209
00:20:27,166 --> 00:20:29,445
I need to make preparations for tomorrow.

210
00:20:40,086 --> 00:20:41,605
Stop.

211
00:20:45,966 --> 00:20:47,325
Seyit.

212
00:20:49,846 --> 00:20:51,805
Go inform Claudius.

213
00:20:52,406 --> 00:20:54,765
I have important things to tell him.

214
00:20:57,246 --> 00:20:58,925
Here we go.

215
00:21:08,486 --> 00:21:10,245
I make beef roasting.

216
00:21:10,566 --> 00:21:13,325
And she makes bulghur.

217
00:21:13,606 --> 00:21:16,165
Her job is easier. It's not fair.

218
00:21:17,926 --> 00:21:20,205
Oh come on. Fatma

219
00:21:20,646 --> 00:21:23,085
Halime is just learning this stuff.

220
00:21:24,686 --> 00:21:27,245
Even this job is too hard for her.

221
00:21:27,886 --> 00:21:29,245
No, it's not hard.

222
00:21:29,606 --> 00:21:31,165
I'm a quick learner.

223
00:21:31,286 --> 00:21:32,605
Oh really?

224
00:21:37,046 --> 00:21:39,045
I'm supposed to add water, right?

225
00:21:39,206 --> 00:21:40,925
How much water should I add?

226
00:21:41,006 --> 00:21:42,405
Well...

227
00:21:42,966 --> 00:21:44,845
I've just taught you.

228
00:21:46,446 --> 00:21:50,405
I'm not saying anything because
Bala Hatun told me to be easy on her.

229
00:21:50,726 --> 00:21:52,285
Look at the bottle she took!

230
00:21:53,606 --> 00:21:56,485
Halime, my dear!
Halime, my dear...

231
00:21:57,886 --> 00:22:01,245
Only that much water for that bulghur?

232
00:22:02,766 --> 00:22:05,805
You know? Do you get it?

233
00:22:11,046 --> 00:22:12,085
You don't get it.

234
00:22:12,166 --> 00:22:15,045
Do you think it's enough?

235
00:22:17,446 --> 00:22:19,805
Halime, Halime.

236
00:22:27,526 --> 00:22:29,805
That water isn't enough.

237
00:22:31,006 --> 00:22:34,445
You need to pour until the water gets above.

238
00:22:38,406 --> 00:22:39,925
Well...

239
00:22:40,086 --> 00:22:43,405
My beef roasting will be
overcooked because of you!

240
00:22:44,406 --> 00:22:45,885
Sister.

241
00:22:46,246 --> 00:22:48,045
You don't want to upset me, right?

242
00:22:48,366 --> 00:22:51,925
I just don't want to upset my mother and father.

243
00:22:52,446 --> 00:22:54,245
Not to make them starve.

244
00:22:54,446 --> 00:22:57,685
If I don't help you, we will die of hunger.

245
00:23:02,486 --> 00:23:04,885
Halime, oil!

246
00:23:05,606 --> 00:23:06,925
Oil, Halime!

247
00:23:07,286 --> 00:23:08,165
Oil.

248
00:23:08,806 --> 00:23:11,925
-Oh I forgot. Oil.
-Yes.

249
00:23:13,046 --> 00:23:14,765
I'm supposed to add salt, right?

250
00:23:14,846 --> 00:23:17,325
Yes, Halime.
Hurry, hurry.

251
00:23:17,566 --> 00:23:19,085
Hurry, Halime!

252
00:23:19,166 --> 00:23:20,925
Mine is about to be overcooked.

253
00:23:32,086 --> 00:23:35,125
My kitchen has turned into a battlefield!

254
00:23:35,526 --> 00:23:38,245
Give me that roller, sister.

255
00:23:39,366 --> 00:23:40,845
Thanks. Ghazi!

256
00:23:41,606 --> 00:23:43,845
You naughty boy, Ghazi!

257
00:23:43,886 --> 00:23:46,445
You put this competition thing in their minds!

258
00:23:46,726 --> 00:23:48,485
Competition is good, mother.

259
00:23:48,766 --> 00:23:50,765
Our stomachs will be filled.

260
00:23:50,886 --> 00:23:54,445
Right?
Like your stomach has never been filled!

261
00:23:54,766 --> 00:23:56,285
Like father like son.

262
00:23:58,046 --> 00:24:01,005
I was so hungry, Ghazi. Well thought.

263
00:24:01,486 --> 00:24:05,565
Don't worry.
I will teach you how to do it.

264
00:24:05,926 --> 00:24:09,085
Don't be worrying, brother.

265
00:24:09,686 --> 00:24:11,085
Mother.

266
00:24:12,806 --> 00:24:14,925
Come, my girl.

267
00:24:15,286 --> 00:24:18,005
They are not cooking but fighting.

268
00:24:19,406 --> 00:24:21,885
Give it to me, Halime!

269
00:24:22,526 --> 00:24:24,205
My Allah!

270
00:24:26,486 --> 00:24:28,205
Give me.

271
00:24:35,966 --> 00:24:37,365
-Mother.
-Yes?

272
00:24:37,726 --> 00:24:40,845
Do you know why my father
is having a council tomorrow?

273
00:24:40,886 --> 00:24:42,645
Everybody is wondering.

274
00:24:43,646 --> 00:24:44,845
I don't know, my dear.

275
00:24:45,046 --> 00:24:48,565
But Osman Bey has been thoughtful for days.

276
00:24:50,726 --> 00:24:53,485
After the council, all of
us will know, God willing.

277
00:24:53,686 --> 00:24:55,285
God willing.

278
00:24:57,006 --> 00:24:58,245
Allah is Eternal!

279
00:24:58,366 --> 00:24:59,285
Allah is The Righteous!

280
00:24:59,366 --> 00:25:04,165
-Allah is Eternal!
-Allah is The Righteous!

281
00:25:04,166 --> 00:25:05,965
Peace be upon you.

282
00:25:07,926 --> 00:25:10,965
-Peace be upon you too.
-Peace be upon you too, sergeant Aykurt.

283
00:25:11,446 --> 00:25:13,725
What are you doing here?

284
00:25:13,846 --> 00:25:15,685
-We are forging.
-We are forging.

285
00:25:15,886 --> 00:25:17,845
Praise be. Praise be.

286
00:25:18,166 --> 00:25:22,085
These brave alps are the sons
of a bey who we appreciate.

287
00:25:22,206 --> 00:25:26,045
-Praise be.
-They're very interested in horses.

288
00:25:26,526 --> 00:25:30,805
Well... I called you so they
could learn from the best.

289
00:25:31,206 --> 00:25:32,485
Hay Praise be.

290
00:25:32,486 --> 00:25:38,085
So, you are interested in the friend
and companion of Turks, the horses, huh?

291
00:25:38,606 --> 00:25:43,365
Then follow me and I will
teach you everything I know.

292
00:25:43,366 --> 00:25:44,925
Come on.

293
00:25:45,286 --> 00:25:47,445
Come with me.

294
00:25:48,886 --> 00:25:54,965
Hay Praise be.

295
00:25:54,966 --> 00:26:01,525
They say Allah created humans
from soil and horses from the wind.

296
00:26:01,526 --> 00:26:03,925
Can an Alp be without a companion? No.

297
00:26:04,246 --> 00:26:06,925
Does Osman Bey have a companion?

298
00:26:06,926 --> 00:26:09,325
You are looking right at it.

299
00:26:13,246 --> 00:26:14,805
The other horses neigh.

300
00:26:14,806 --> 00:26:16,765
Why doesn't this horse neigh?

301
00:26:16,766 --> 00:26:22,725
It looks quiet but speaks with
its heart. Look into its eyes.

302
00:26:22,726 --> 00:26:26,725
It knows a lot, it doesn't say a thing.
It travels far, but it does not complain.

303
00:26:26,726 --> 00:26:31,325
If you talk to it, it listens to you.

304
00:26:31,326 --> 00:26:32,965
How will we talk to it?

305
00:26:32,966 --> 00:26:34,965
Tell me, what is your name?

306
00:26:34,966 --> 00:26:36,445
MelikShah Alp.

307
00:26:36,446 --> 00:26:38,645
Praise be MelikShah.

308
00:26:38,646 --> 00:26:39,805
Well-said.

309
00:26:39,806 --> 00:26:42,645
We read the soul of the horse.

310
00:26:42,646 --> 00:26:44,365
We look into its eyes.

311
00:26:44,366 --> 00:26:48,165
Are its ears upright? Is its tail calm?

312
00:26:48,486 --> 00:26:51,885
If you know how to look, it gives you answers.

313
00:26:51,886 --> 00:26:55,845
Then we speak with them.

314
00:26:56,086 --> 00:26:58,885
Watch carefully, MelikShah, learn.

315
00:26:59,286 --> 00:27:04,405
Now this horse came from the
road and is tired. We will groom it.

316
00:27:04,646 --> 00:27:07,205
What happens if we don't groom it?

317
00:27:07,246 --> 00:27:10,045
Good question, Alparslan Alp.

318
00:27:10,046 --> 00:27:14,645
If we don't groom it, the horse's
fur gets tangled. Its skin itches.

319
00:27:14,646 --> 00:27:16,645
It won't even walk.

320
00:27:16,646 --> 00:27:21,245
And if the saddle hurts its
back, it won't listen to you.

321
00:27:21,246 --> 00:27:23,525
It won't even look at you.

322
00:27:24,206 --> 00:27:26,085
Now..

323
00:27:26,086 --> 00:27:28,805
Now we start from the neck.

324
00:27:31,006 --> 00:27:32,605
Then the back.

325
00:27:32,606 --> 00:27:34,085
Then here.

326
00:27:34,566 --> 00:27:39,645
Most importantly, these thin legs.

327
00:27:40,206 --> 00:27:42,245
We also groom the legs.

328
00:27:44,606 --> 00:27:48,605
If you approach it from behind,
it will kick you in the chest.

329
00:28:04,566 --> 00:28:10,205
The companion of the valiants,
the noble brother of the Alp.

330
00:28:10,206 --> 00:28:16,205
Sometimes it is his secret keeper,
never returns from battle without him.

331
00:28:16,206 --> 00:28:21,165
We go on the road of war,
and we swear with our hearts.

332
00:28:21,166 --> 00:28:27,005
It bows its head and listens to your
words if you don't pull the reins too hard.

333
00:28:27,206 --> 00:28:32,245
Its hooves break stones,
its mane falls over its face.

334
00:28:32,286 --> 00:28:35,005
If you care for it well, it shines like a star.

335
00:28:35,006 --> 00:28:42,685
The crescent moon appears in its noble eyes.

336
00:29:15,886 --> 00:29:21,445
You prepared a welcome suitable
for a Byzantine nobleman, Claudius.

337
00:29:21,566 --> 00:29:23,925
I have always been kind to my friends.

338
00:29:24,846 --> 00:29:27,805
Especially to those who bring me information.

339
00:29:28,206 --> 00:29:29,765
Sit down.

340
00:29:44,566 --> 00:29:47,925
You and I share the same fate.

341
00:29:48,526 --> 00:29:51,405
I am a sharp sword...

342
00:29:52,206 --> 00:29:54,885
...you are a long spear.

343
00:29:54,886 --> 00:29:57,805
We are now on the same path.

344
00:29:58,086 --> 00:30:00,205
I believe that.

345
00:30:01,006 --> 00:30:04,925
Now tell me what you know, Yigit Bey.

346
00:30:05,206 --> 00:30:07,725
Osman Bey will hold a council.

347
00:30:09,326 --> 00:30:14,485
He invited all the Beys.

348
00:30:16,086 --> 00:30:18,485
As you know...

349
00:30:18,486 --> 00:30:21,685
..when Osman Bey calls for a council...

350
00:30:21,886 --> 00:30:25,765
...a storm follows it.

351
00:30:26,886 --> 00:30:31,485
You need to learn what
decisions are made in that council.

352
00:30:31,486 --> 00:30:33,405
I will learn.

353
00:30:33,846 --> 00:30:36,205
I will learn.

354
00:30:36,566 --> 00:30:40,085
Once we start working together...

355
00:30:40,166 --> 00:30:44,285
...we will defeat Osman together.

356
00:30:45,486 --> 00:30:48,685
But in return..

357
00:30:49,766 --> 00:30:52,965
...you will
give me gold and the land of Goynuk.

358
00:30:53,606 --> 00:30:56,045
And I will settle my tribe there.

359
00:30:56,046 --> 00:30:57,805
"My" tribe?

360
00:30:58,286 --> 00:31:01,725
I guess you mean your brother's tribe.

361
00:31:05,966 --> 00:31:09,485
Or you will bring your brother down.

362
00:31:12,366 --> 00:31:14,045
Good.

363
00:31:16,166 --> 00:31:18,445
Do we have a deal, Claudius?

364
00:31:18,446 --> 00:31:20,365
We do.

365
00:31:20,686 --> 00:31:25,845
You will get everything you
want when Osman's rule is over.

366
00:31:25,846 --> 00:31:27,765
God willing.

367
00:31:29,046 --> 00:31:30,885
Here.

368
00:31:51,926 --> 00:31:54,605
Your burden must be heavy, right, my Osman?

369
00:31:54,606 --> 00:31:57,325
Is it the burden of the tomorrow's council?

370
00:31:57,646 --> 00:32:01,645
My burden is heavy. It is.

371
00:32:01,886 --> 00:32:04,085
I have a long way to go, Bala.

372
00:32:06,046 --> 00:32:09,565
Whenever I come to you, whenever I come here...

373
00:32:09,726 --> 00:32:11,245
...I forget about my burden.

374
00:32:11,246 --> 00:32:13,965
I always feel better here.

375
00:32:14,806 --> 00:32:17,885
I wish I could help you more.

376
00:32:18,686 --> 00:32:23,125
Look, today another one of our
dreams will come true. Dark Osman.

377
00:32:23,126 --> 00:32:24,405
What is it?

378
00:32:24,406 --> 00:32:29,005
Our daughters have been in the
kitchen since morning, cooking for you.

379
00:32:29,166 --> 00:32:31,805
Really? They are cooking for me?

380
00:32:31,806 --> 00:32:35,605
Who else would it be? They are
preparing a table for their father.

381
00:32:35,606 --> 00:32:40,245
They are competing with each other
too. We dreamed of this so much.

382
00:32:40,246 --> 00:32:41,725
Right, Bala.

383
00:32:44,286 --> 00:32:48,365
All the things we thought impossible
are coming true one by one.

384
00:32:49,966 --> 00:32:54,085
You used to tell me,
"Servants plan, but fate laughs."

385
00:32:54,086 --> 00:32:56,565
Right? Do you remember?

386
00:32:56,686 --> 00:32:58,445
Right.

387
00:32:59,366 --> 00:33:01,245
I said that.

388
00:33:02,166 --> 00:33:04,125
If only you could see, Osman.

389
00:33:04,126 --> 00:33:08,685
When I saw them happy and
together, I thanked my Allah.

390
00:33:09,246 --> 00:33:11,845
Our dreams are coming true.

391
00:33:11,846 --> 00:33:14,285
You once opposed me.

392
00:33:14,326 --> 00:33:18,285
You wanted to leave me
because of a wound, remember?

393
00:33:18,686 --> 00:33:23,965
I told you, we would have a daughter, we would
have children, and our family would grow.

394
00:33:23,966 --> 00:33:25,325
You see?

395
00:33:25,326 --> 00:33:27,965
Now they are cooking for

396
00:33:28,806 --> 00:33:30,805
Thanks to Allah.

397
00:33:30,886 --> 00:33:32,405
Fortunately, my Osman.

398
00:33:34,326 --> 00:33:35,725
Yes, fortunately.

399
00:33:42,766 --> 00:33:48,285
Alps, now all of you will
pull yourselves together.

400
00:33:52,766 --> 00:33:54,325
Alps.

401
00:33:54,326 --> 00:33:56,205
Let me tell you this.

402
00:33:56,206 --> 00:34:00,445
Turgut Ghazi will break your bones.

403
00:34:00,446 --> 00:34:02,365
You won't even be able to sleep.

404
00:34:02,366 --> 00:34:07,165
He will make you train day and night.

405
00:34:11,286 --> 00:34:12,844
Peace be upon you

406
00:34:12,846 --> 00:34:15,125
Peace be upon you too

407
00:34:15,286 --> 00:34:16,965
Come, Turgut Ghazi.

408
00:34:16,966 --> 00:34:18,685
Thank you.

409
00:34:20,326 --> 00:34:21,764
Sit, Alps.

410
00:34:29,686 --> 00:34:31,485
Alps...

411
00:34:32,886 --> 00:34:36,645
Today, what brought
you defeat during the drill...

412
00:34:36,726 --> 00:34:40,685
...was the weakness of your brotherhood bond.

413
00:34:40,886 --> 00:34:44,525
There are brothers who put others in trouble.

414
00:34:44,926 --> 00:34:49,085
And there are brothers who bring victories.

415
00:34:50,326 --> 00:34:52,205
Now..

416
00:34:52,206 --> 00:34:54,764
...I will tell you the story of...

417
00:34:54,766 --> 00:35:00,325
...two brave brothers who
always fought together.

418
00:35:00,326 --> 00:35:02,445
One time..

419
00:35:02,726 --> 00:35:06,565
...I heard it from the late Suleyman Shah.

420
00:35:08,726 --> 00:35:11,605
This story has almost
everything, nothing is left out.

421
00:35:11,646 --> 00:35:14,245
It has all the truth, there
is not a single lie in it.

422
00:35:14,246 --> 00:35:16,925
It is called a story...

423
00:35:17,366 --> 00:35:19,765
...but it is real.

424
00:35:21,046 --> 00:35:23,045
During their time...

425
00:35:23,046 --> 00:35:25,605
..there were two brothers...

426
00:35:25,606 --> 00:35:29,845
...who founded the Seljuk State, which
was the strongest and biggest state...

427
00:35:29,846 --> 00:35:32,165
..in the world.

428
00:35:32,606 --> 00:35:36,845
One of them was the master of
politics, the Sultan of Sultans...

429
00:35:36,846 --> 00:35:38,285
...Tugrul Bey...

430
00:35:38,286 --> 00:35:42,365
The other was his older brother,
the commander of commanders...

431
00:35:42,366 --> 00:35:44,925
...the master of battlefields...

432
00:35:44,926 --> 00:35:47,565
...the one who could break
swords with bare hands...

433
00:35:47,566 --> 00:35:49,445
...Cagri Bey.

434
00:35:50,686 --> 00:35:55,845
At that time, the land was watered with blood.

435
00:35:56,206 --> 00:35:59,085
As the earth shook...

436
00:35:59,086 --> 00:36:03,245
...the blue sky turned the color of blood.

437
00:36:03,966 --> 00:36:08,645
While every nation
fought for its own survival...

438
00:36:08,646 --> 00:36:13,245
...the foundation and
rise of the Seljuk State...

439
00:36:13,606 --> 00:36:17,165
...were tied to the lives of these two brothers.

440
00:36:17,286 --> 00:36:22,650
After their father passed
away, Cagri Bey made a

441
00:36:22,662 --> 00:36:28,805
decision that was very rare
and shocked everyone deeply.

442
00:36:28,966 --> 00:36:31,685
What decision did he make, Turgut Ghazi?

443
00:36:34,206 --> 00:36:38,802
Even though the throne
rightfully belonged to Cagri

444
00:36:38,814 --> 00:36:43,245
Bey, he gave it to his
younger brother Tugrul Bey.

445
00:36:45,206 --> 00:36:49,285
How did he defeat his nafs, Turgut Ghazi?

446
00:36:49,286 --> 00:36:52,125
How did he not want to be the ruler?

447
00:36:52,126 --> 00:36:56,485
Cagri Bey was a leader
who was always victorious.

448
00:36:56,486 --> 00:36:59,725
He was the master of battlefields.

449
00:37:00,086 --> 00:37:05,725
No one could stand against his
sword. No one could stand against him.

450
00:37:05,726 --> 00:37:10,525
Tugrul Bey was a skilled ruler...

451
00:37:10,526 --> 00:37:15,725
...a brave Sultan who was a master of politics.

452
00:37:15,926 --> 00:37:21,365
They never wanted something for themselves.

453
00:37:21,366 --> 00:37:28,165
Tugrul Bey's wisdom and Cagri Bey's
sword gained victories one after another.

454
00:37:28,166 --> 00:37:31,285
They rode across continents.

455
00:37:31,446 --> 00:37:36,165
When war started and the storm came...

456
00:37:37,046 --> 00:37:41,245
...when they shot the Seljuk arrows to the sky..

457
00:37:41,286 --> 00:37:44,005
...they could even block out the sun.

458
00:37:44,886 --> 00:37:49,325
The dark ground would get even darker.

459
00:37:49,606 --> 00:37:54,405
The warriors from Turkistan,
riding fast horses like eagles...

460
00:37:54,406 --> 00:37:58,685
...ripped the hearts of their enemies!

461
00:37:58,686 --> 00:38:02,205
Hay Praise be.

462
00:38:02,326 --> 00:38:06,325
These two brothers, these two noble Beys...

463
00:38:06,326 --> 00:38:12,445
...chose to be united and strong
instead of fighting each other.

464
00:38:12,446 --> 00:38:17,765
They always chose to cover each other's flaws.

465
00:38:17,806 --> 00:38:23,565
One became the mind of the
state, the other the sword of justice.

466
00:38:23,566 --> 00:38:30,605
Everyone in the world heard about them. They
walked together for the cause of Islam...

467
00:38:30,806 --> 00:38:33,685
...and built a great state.

468
00:38:34,446 --> 00:38:41,685
They never gave up their roots
or the legacy of their ancestors.

469
00:38:41,686 --> 00:38:47,165
While Sultan Tugrul built a
civilization in the capital city of Rey...

470
00:38:47,166 --> 00:38:53,885
...Cagri Bey stayed in Khorasan
and trained the army in his tribe.

471
00:38:54,046 --> 00:39:01,485
These two selfless men
established that great state this way.

472
00:39:01,486 --> 00:39:05,605
Praise be.

473
00:39:06,046 --> 00:39:09,565
What you should learn from this story is...

474
00:39:09,926 --> 00:39:14,525
...always be united and stay strong.

475
00:39:14,526 --> 00:39:19,125
War is not only won on the battlefield.

476
00:39:19,166 --> 00:39:23,525
True victory comes from
brave hearts that beat together...

477
00:39:23,606 --> 00:39:26,845
...that never ask for...

478
00:39:29,126 --> 00:39:31,565
...something for itselves.

479
00:39:31,566 --> 00:39:34,085
Yes, Turgut Ghazi.

480
00:39:43,046 --> 00:39:44,325
Alaeddin, Gonca.

481
00:39:44,326 --> 00:39:45,165
My Bey.

482
00:39:45,166 --> 00:39:48,445
Where are your sisters?

483
00:39:48,446 --> 00:39:49,725
Don't even ask, father.

484
00:39:49,726 --> 00:39:54,285
They'll come now

485
00:39:55,806 --> 00:40:00,565
I swear I did nothing wrong, my Bey.

486
00:40:00,566 --> 00:40:03,045
Alright then, let's sit.

487
00:40:04,526 --> 00:40:07,495
In the name of Allah, 
the merciful, the compassionate.

488
00:40:11,646 --> 00:40:15,045
I told you. We're late.
Our father is waiting for us.

489
00:40:15,126 --> 00:40:16,965
It's not my fault.

490
00:40:17,846 --> 00:40:20,485
It was you who kept interrupting me, sister.

491
00:40:21,086 --> 00:40:23,605
Father, look. I made bulghur for you.

492
00:40:26,246 --> 00:40:28,805
Yes, raw bulghur.

493
00:40:29,126 --> 00:40:31,845
Taste my roasting.

494
00:40:33,806 --> 00:40:35,525
It's perfectly cooked.

495
00:40:50,806 --> 00:40:52,245
We will see.

496
00:40:52,446 --> 00:40:55,885
Bala, you see? Our daughters cook for us now.

497
00:40:56,006 --> 00:40:57,045
Yes.

498
00:40:57,126 --> 00:40:59,725
Praise be to my girls.

499
00:41:03,766 --> 00:41:05,445
Let's eat.

500
00:41:06,566 --> 00:41:08,645
Let's eat and make a choice.

501
00:41:10,926 --> 00:41:13,965
You leave it. Ulgen, let's do it together.

502
00:41:15,406 --> 00:41:17,165
Wait, wait.

503
00:41:17,686 --> 00:41:20,445
You sit beside me. Come on.

504
00:41:22,166 --> 00:41:25,205
Well, we'll eat together.
We'll eat together.

505
00:41:26,406 --> 00:41:28,565
You see, hatun?

506
00:41:28,966 --> 00:41:31,245
We have got forgotten already.

507
00:41:31,966 --> 00:41:35,245
Just wait, Alaaddin. Don't be jealous.

508
00:41:36,126 --> 00:41:39,965
He's implying Fatma, my dear.
Don't mess with my girls. Alaaddin Bey.

509
00:41:40,566 --> 00:41:43,405
Well, mother... You already call me Bey?

510
00:41:45,326 --> 00:41:47,285
Don't mess with my daughters.

511
00:42:00,166 --> 00:42:03,205
Here we go. In the name of Allah,
the merciful, the compassionate.

512
00:42:05,526 --> 00:42:07,885
Let's start with this.

513
00:42:41,686 --> 00:42:43,645
Alaaddin.

514
00:42:45,566 --> 00:42:48,165
How do you like, father? Is it well cooked?

515
00:42:58,686 --> 00:43:00,325
Very good.

516
00:43:04,166 --> 00:43:05,565
Very good.

517
00:43:09,686 --> 00:43:13,125
The meat is nicely cooked,
sister. Thanks for cooking.

518
00:43:13,846 --> 00:43:17,805
Of course it is, brother.
Because I made the roasting.

519
00:43:18,446 --> 00:43:23,005
If you want to see Halime's
skills, taste the bulghur.

520
00:43:25,046 --> 00:43:29,925
Hey, you've already started
teaching your sister? Good girl.

521
00:43:33,526 --> 00:43:35,085
Well..

522
00:43:35,446 --> 00:43:38,325
Train her to fight. Teach her to cook.

523
00:43:38,446 --> 00:43:40,565
-And?
-Make her memorize the Quran surahs.

524
00:43:40,886 --> 00:43:41,925
And

525
00:43:42,166 --> 00:43:44,045
Do I have to deal with you?

526
00:43:46,726 --> 00:43:47,805
Whatever.

527
00:43:48,366 --> 00:43:50,165
There is nothing to do.

528
00:43:50,806 --> 00:43:52,685
I have to teach, I guess.

529
00:43:54,686 --> 00:43:57,245
-You have to.
-I have to teach.

530
00:44:10,406 --> 00:44:13,765
The bulghur is uncooked.

531
00:44:29,046 --> 00:44:31,205
And the meat is too hard.

532
00:44:34,846 --> 00:44:36,605
Why didn't you tell us?

533
00:44:38,246 --> 00:44:42,125
No, my dear. It's the best
meal I have ever tasted.

534
00:44:42,126 --> 00:44:43,805
Right?

535
00:44:44,366 --> 00:44:46,725
Yes, yes. Very nice.

536
00:44:57,646 --> 00:45:00,325
Come closer to me.

537
00:45:00,766 --> 00:45:02,725
What matters is you cooked them.

538
00:45:02,766 --> 00:45:06,365
Besides, you will know better by practicing.

539
00:45:06,686 --> 00:45:07,805
Ulgen.

540
00:45:08,006 --> 00:45:11,685
My daughter will cook the
meals of the tribe from now on.

541
00:45:15,846 --> 00:45:18,045
Oh no, my Bey.

542
00:45:18,326 --> 00:45:21,245
My kitchen has turned into a battlefield.

543
00:45:21,446 --> 00:45:22,645
What?

544
00:45:22,926 --> 00:45:25,325
-Sister Ulgen!
-I mean it.

545
00:45:33,406 --> 00:45:37,045
Halime, I told you to add
water. Didn't you do it?

546
00:45:37,686 --> 00:45:41,325
My roasting got overcooked
because I was trying to help you.

547
00:45:45,486 --> 00:45:47,205
Well, my Bey...

548
00:45:48,326 --> 00:45:50,485
Who do you think won?

549
00:45:55,686 --> 00:45:59,245
Well... Well..

550
00:45:59,486 --> 00:46:02,405
Sisterhood won today.

551
00:46:02,646 --> 00:46:07,885
But I don't know what
happens next time. Alright?

552
00:46:09,406 --> 00:46:11,005
-Fine.
-Here we go.

553
00:46:11,726 --> 00:46:14,845
-Let's eat.
-Alaaddin, eat.

554
00:46:16,766 --> 00:46:18,765
I will eat, my Bey.

555
00:46:21,126 --> 00:46:22,685
Thank you, hatun.

556
00:46:36,566 --> 00:46:39,525
I'm starving. I'm starving.
Where is your mother, Ghazi?

557
00:46:39,686 --> 00:46:42,445
Where are the meals Ghazi? I'm starving!

558
00:46:43,206 --> 00:46:47,045
Father, have you ever been full?

559
00:46:53,766 --> 00:46:55,285
Don't hit him.

560
00:46:55,446 --> 00:46:57,525
The boy will be stupid!

561
00:46:58,486 --> 00:47:04,325
A spoon can't make him stupid.
They hit harder woods on my head.

562
00:47:07,206 --> 00:47:10,525
I see... That's why you are like this.

563
00:47:12,166 --> 00:47:14,805
I thought Allah created you like that.

564
00:47:15,406 --> 00:47:18,925
Give it to me.

565
00:47:20,766 --> 00:47:22,365
Come on, come on.

566
00:47:23,206 --> 00:47:26,285
What did you mean by saying that?

567
00:47:26,566 --> 00:47:30,965
I didn't mean to say anything, Cerkutay.
Don't mess with me. I feel terrible.

568
00:47:54,806 --> 00:47:57,485
-In the name of Allah.
-In the name of Allah.

569
00:48:22,006 --> 00:48:23,245
Ulgen.

570
00:48:25,486 --> 00:48:28,165
Do we live in a desert, Ulgen?

571
00:48:28,566 --> 00:48:31,205
Is there no water in the wells?

572
00:48:31,606 --> 00:48:35,565
Did all the bottles get broken?
This isn't a meal but rock!

573
00:48:35,566 --> 00:48:40,685
This needs to be boiled. It's like
rock! My teeth almost got broken!

574
00:48:41,086 --> 00:48:44,245
Father, it wasn't my mother who...

575
00:48:44,806 --> 00:48:47,325
What do you mean by saying that, Cerkutay?

576
00:48:47,566 --> 00:48:49,565
Don't you like the meal I cooked?

577
00:48:53,446 --> 00:48:55,045
-I like it.
-Yes.

578
00:48:55,126 --> 00:48:59,205
I like it. How can I not like the meal you cook?

579
00:49:00,006 --> 00:49:02,325
Good. You eat all of it then.

580
00:49:02,526 --> 00:49:06,485
Here. Take it. Come on, eat.

581
00:49:07,646 --> 00:49:10,325
Enjoy your meal.

582
00:49:14,806 --> 00:49:18,605
Pour water, Ghazi.
Pour some water.

583
00:49:18,806 --> 00:49:22,125
Well... Great meals for my Bey!

584
00:49:26,686 --> 00:49:28,245
I can't swallow.

585
00:51:00,006 --> 00:51:03,885
Sufficient for us is Allah, and
He is the best Disposer of affairs.

586
00:51:05,726 --> 00:51:09,405
Sufficient for us is Allah, and
He is the best Disposer of affairs.

587
00:51:35,766 --> 00:51:43,605
Help. Help. Help me, my Allah.

588
00:51:44,046 --> 00:51:49,325
Help, help, help.

589
00:51:54,926 --> 00:51:56,565
Help.

590
00:52:32,166 --> 00:52:34,860
I seek refuge in Allah
from the outcast Shaitan. In

591
00:52:34,872 --> 00:52:37,525
the name of Allah, The
Compassionate, The Merciful.

592
00:52:37,566 --> 00:52:39,365
Help me, my Allah.

593
00:52:39,846 --> 00:52:41,485
Help me, my Allah.

594
00:52:42,726 --> 00:52:45,045
Help me, my Allah.

595
00:53:42,006 --> 00:53:43,885
Turgut Ghazi.

596
00:53:44,766 --> 00:53:47,685
No. Sit.

597
00:54:01,006 --> 00:54:06,805
What? Couldn't you sleep either?

598
00:54:07,766 --> 00:54:10,045
When there is moonlight.

599
00:54:11,646 --> 00:54:14,285
...I can't sleep, Osman.

600
00:54:19,886 --> 00:54:23,045
Tell me. Why didn't you sleep?

601
00:54:25,046 --> 00:54:27,605
I had such a nightmare...

602
00:54:30,246 --> 00:54:32,885
I was trapped inside the walls.

603
00:54:34,686 --> 00:54:40,245
My hands and feet were chained.

604
00:54:43,486 --> 00:54:45,605
I tried to get out of there.

605
00:54:47,286 --> 00:54:50,165
Did you get out?
-No.

606
00:54:53,006 --> 00:54:54,565
I couldn't.

607
00:54:56,406 --> 00:54:58,245
I started hitting.

608
00:54:59,766 --> 00:55:01,605
I tried to break them.

609
00:55:03,326 --> 00:55:06,285
I felt some fire when I broke.

610
00:55:06,766 --> 00:55:08,565
Such a fire..

611
00:55:12,366 --> 00:55:15,445
May Allah make it herald the good.

612
00:55:21,846 --> 00:55:25,485
What burns you?

613
00:55:26,966 --> 00:55:32,325
The fire or the burden of
the state on your shoulders?

614
00:55:34,246 --> 00:55:37,005
My father once told me.

615
00:55:38,726 --> 00:55:40,885
"When you become a Bey

616
00:55:42,766 --> 00:55:44,725
...you will understand me."

617
00:55:47,166 --> 00:55:48,845
This burden of the state...

618
00:55:50,006 --> 00:55:51,965
This shirt of fire.

619
00:55:54,646 --> 00:55:56,565
To reach our goals

620
00:55:57,046 --> 00:55:59,485
..I have to pay too much.

621
00:56:10,326 --> 00:56:11,885
This axe..

622
00:56:12,686 --> 00:56:15,605
You know how this axe is made, right?

623
00:56:17,126 --> 00:56:18,445
By forging.

624
00:56:19,286 --> 00:56:21,565
It becomes like this by getting hits.

625
00:56:26,046 --> 00:56:29,485
Blows one after another inside the flames.

626
00:56:30,206 --> 00:56:32,565
It gets cool in the water.

627
00:56:34,886 --> 00:56:37,045
But then it burns again.

628
00:56:38,406 --> 00:56:41,125
How could it be so hard and strong...

629
00:56:43,846 --> 00:56:46,445
..if it didn't suffer so much?

630
00:56:50,686 --> 00:56:52,045
And you?

631
00:56:53,326 --> 00:56:55,685
If you hadn't suffered all those things.

632
00:56:56,006 --> 00:56:59,205
If you hadn't burned in flames,
what would have happened?

633
00:57:02,686 --> 00:57:05,485
I don't care about my own suffering.

634
00:57:10,806 --> 00:57:16,405
I'm thinking about the decision I
need to make in the council tomorrow.

635
00:57:17,046 --> 00:57:19,285
I care about my people.

636
00:57:21,766 --> 00:57:23,565
Well..

637
00:57:25,366 --> 00:57:26,845
We need conquests.

638
00:57:28,566 --> 00:57:30,845
But my people are just regaining strength.

639
00:57:32,446 --> 00:57:34,685
That's why I'm thinking of my people.

640
00:57:36,206 --> 00:57:38,805
Suffering and reward.

641
00:57:39,406 --> 00:57:41,565
Blessing and trouble.

642
00:57:42,046 --> 00:57:45,605
They only come from Allah.

643
00:57:53,846 --> 00:57:56,685
You need to move forward, Osman.

644
00:57:57,486 --> 00:58:02,165
You made many enemies kneel until this day.

645
00:58:02,166 --> 00:58:07,165
Of course, many more enemies
will set traps against you on this path.

646
00:58:09,046 --> 00:58:11,805
As they set traps...

647
00:58:11,806 --> 00:58:17,885
...you and your descendants will
make history with Allah's permission.

648
00:58:19,966 --> 00:58:21,485
God willing.

649
00:58:21,486 --> 00:58:24,365
God willing. God willing.

650
00:58:26,846 --> 00:58:28,365
This is...

651
00:58:28,366 --> 00:58:31,005
...a test for all of us, Osman.

652
00:58:31,006 --> 00:58:33,005
All of us.

653
00:58:33,246 --> 00:58:35,445
Those who pass the test...

654
00:58:35,966 --> 00:58:39,205
...will reach the target.

655
00:58:44,766 --> 00:58:46,485
Come on now.

656
00:58:46,566 --> 00:58:48,645
Get up now.

657
00:58:55,006 --> 00:58:56,805
Your heart...

658
00:58:56,806 --> 00:58:59,605
...is as big as the state.

659
00:59:01,966 --> 00:59:04,605
Do what your heart tells you to do.

660
00:59:05,606 --> 00:59:07,365
As long as my Allah...

661
00:59:07,966 --> 00:59:10,965
..allows me..

662
00:59:11,166 --> 00:59:13,645
...I will never give up on this path.

663
00:59:17,246 --> 00:59:19,445
Praise be to you.

664
00:59:26,246 --> 00:59:30,005
We will reignite the Byzantine
fire on the frontiers, Sofia.

665
00:59:30,006 --> 00:59:34,325
We will root Turks out from the frontiers.

666
00:59:34,486 --> 00:59:36,405
First, Osman.

667
00:59:36,406 --> 00:59:38,005
My alliance with Osman...

668
00:59:38,006 --> 00:59:41,885
...did not give me anything.

669
00:59:41,966 --> 00:59:46,605
I even lost what I had in
my hands, Great Emperor.

670
00:59:47,046 --> 00:59:49,245
I am at your service.

671
00:59:49,446 --> 00:59:52,285
What is your order for me?

672
00:59:55,726 --> 00:59:57,485
First...

673
00:59:57,486 --> 01:00:01,965
I order you to leave the past behind, Sofia.

674
01:00:24,966 --> 01:00:27,765
This dastard...

675
01:00:28,566 --> 01:00:32,085
...must be locked in a dungeon, Great Emperor.

676
01:00:32,886 --> 01:00:35,645
You were the one who betrayed, Sofia.

677
01:00:36,046 --> 01:00:37,845
If I am here..

678
01:00:37,846 --> 01:00:40,965
...it's because I am loyal to our Emperor.

679
01:00:41,326 --> 01:00:43,045
Enough!

680
01:00:54,246 --> 01:00:56,565
As we fight with each other...

681
01:00:56,606 --> 01:00:59,325
...Osman gets even stronger!

682
01:01:00,166 --> 01:01:02,205
For the Great Roman Empire

683
01:01:02,206 --> 01:01:05,885
...you will end the enmity between you.

684
01:01:06,326 --> 01:01:09,325
He stole Bursa from me.

685
01:01:09,326 --> 01:01:11,645
Great Emperor.

686
01:01:12,126 --> 01:01:15,525
And you stole my trust in you, Sofia.

687
01:01:17,046 --> 01:01:19,885
But to see Osman suffering in pain...

688
01:01:19,886 --> 01:01:21,725
...I can do anything.

689
01:01:22,246 --> 01:01:24,445
Including giving the throne of Bursa...

690
01:01:24,446 --> 01:01:27,085
..to Sofia.

691
01:01:37,326 --> 01:01:40,485
You will rule Bursa together.

692
01:01:44,486 --> 01:01:47,325
Then we will destroy Osman...

693
01:01:47,486 --> 01:01:53,245
I will also divide his properties
we seize between you two.

694
01:02:02,926 --> 01:02:05,725
As you order.

695
01:02:08,326 --> 01:02:11,245
It is the best time to unite.

696
01:02:13,246 --> 01:02:16,845
Tomorrow, Osman will hold a
council with his Beys tomorrow.

697
01:02:18,726 --> 01:02:21,725
If he is gathering his all Beys...

698
01:02:22,686 --> 01:02:25,765
...he must be after something big.

699
01:02:26,326 --> 01:02:30,125
And it will surely affect Byzantium.

700
01:02:31,206 --> 01:02:34,685
We will find out what will be
talked about there. Don't worry.

701
01:02:34,806 --> 01:02:37,405
I have a spy among them, sir.

702
01:02:37,406 --> 01:02:41,285
Having a spy will be very
useful for us, Claudius.

703
01:02:41,286 --> 01:02:43,445
But it's not enough.

704
01:02:43,526 --> 01:02:48,085
Tomorrow, all the Lords at the
frontiers will gather in the arena.

705
01:02:48,566 --> 01:02:52,165
We will set the great Byzantine fire.

706
01:02:52,166 --> 01:02:56,565
We will awaken the sleeping
Byzantine spirit once again.

707
01:03:19,246 --> 01:03:21,565
Peace be upon you

708
01:03:21,766 --> 01:03:23,885
Peace be upon you too.

709
01:03:25,926 --> 01:03:27,485
Peace be upon you too.

710
01:03:27,486 --> 01:03:29,565
Alaeddin Bey.

711
01:03:30,966 --> 01:03:36,005
Since yesterday, everyone has been
talking about Osman Bey's council.

712
01:03:36,446 --> 01:03:39,325
Do you know the reason for this council?

713
01:03:40,566 --> 01:03:43,525
The Bey speaks at the council, Yigit Bey.

714
01:03:43,526 --> 01:03:46,205
We will all learn together.

715
01:03:48,646 --> 01:03:50,365
Beys...

716
01:03:50,566 --> 01:03:53,445
...the Mongol trouble has
ended, with Allah's help.

717
01:03:53,446 --> 01:03:58,845
Osman Bey will make new
decisions for the people and the state.

718
01:04:00,086 --> 01:04:03,525
The Mongols are gone, but...

719
01:04:03,526 --> 01:04:08,245
...there is disorder in the world, Beys.

720
01:04:08,246 --> 01:04:13,045
I have heard that Turk Beys fight each other.

721
01:04:13,566 --> 01:04:15,765
Germiyan, Karaman.

722
01:04:15,766 --> 01:04:19,485
What will be our place in this war, Beys?

723
01:04:27,086 --> 01:04:31,605
Beys, we are ready for the council.
Osman Bey is waiting for you.

724
01:04:51,966 --> 01:04:53,085
Attention!

725
01:04:53,086 --> 01:04:54,965
Osman Bey!

726
01:04:57,086 --> 01:04:58,045
Peace be upon you

727
01:04:58,046 --> 01:05:01,525
Peace be upon you too.

728
01:05:20,366 --> 01:05:22,725
With Almighty Allah's 99 names..

729
01:05:23,326 --> 01:05:27,325
...Who says "Be", and it is...

730
01:05:27,806 --> 01:05:31,125
...and fills our heart with faith...

731
01:05:31,286 --> 01:05:33,165
...I am opening the council.

732
01:05:33,166 --> 01:05:38,005
In the name of Allah, 
the merciful, the compassionate.

733
01:05:40,646 --> 01:05:41,765
We did not...

734
01:05:41,766 --> 01:05:42,405
We did not..

735
01:05:43,566 --> 01:05:46,125
...have many men before.

736
01:05:46,566 --> 01:05:51,245
But we have sent the infidels
away from these borders.

737
01:05:52,566 --> 01:05:58,245
We were a Beylic, now we are a state.

738
01:06:01,206 --> 01:06:10,045
We will restore this state, which the Mongols
have destroyed, to its former strength.

739
01:06:10,446 --> 01:06:12,605
God willing my Bey.

740
01:06:12,606 --> 01:06:21,005
What strengthens a state is justice
and tradition, but treasure is also needed.

741
01:06:21,966 --> 01:06:25,565
The battle with the Mongols
destroyed our treasure, my Bey.

742
01:06:25,566 --> 01:06:31,925
The nomads have no treasure but patched tents.

743
01:06:31,926 --> 01:06:36,765
How will we make this state strong again?

744
01:06:37,166 --> 01:06:38,725
By fighting

745
01:06:39,886 --> 01:06:44,325
War will open the doors to treasure.

746
01:06:44,326 --> 01:06:51,765
The treasure is in the borders
ruled by the oppression of Byzantium.

747
01:06:51,806 --> 01:06:55,925
The nomads fell into war
without settling anywhere.

748
01:06:55,926 --> 01:06:57,845
We fought.

749
01:06:58,166 --> 01:07:00,805
We destroyed the Mongols with Allah's help.

750
01:07:01,566 --> 01:07:04,365
But the Alps are tired, Osman Bey.

751
01:07:04,366 --> 01:07:05,845
We don't have many Alps.

752
01:07:05,926 --> 01:07:09,605
I worry that this battle may bring us defeat.

753
01:07:09,606 --> 01:07:14,525
What do you mean, Hasan
Bey? A sword rusts in its sheath.

754
01:07:14,526 --> 01:07:18,765
An Alp rests in war.

755
01:07:21,246 --> 01:07:23,445
Wait..

756
01:07:24,486 --> 01:07:25,845
Wait..

757
01:07:25,846 --> 01:07:26,685
Wait...

758
01:07:28,686 --> 01:07:31,045
We are holding a council here.

759
01:07:31,246 --> 01:07:35,325
Here, everyone will say what they wish.

760
01:07:35,766 --> 01:07:38,805
Let the opinions be freed
from the tongue, Koca Bey.

761
01:07:41,926 --> 01:07:45,285
Hasan Bey. Tell us.

762
01:07:46,646 --> 01:07:50,645
The winter has just ended.
The nomads are miserable.

763
01:07:50,886 --> 01:07:56,525
I say let the Alps and
children rejoice with the spring.

764
01:07:56,526 --> 01:08:00,245
Let our horses and sheep
rest in the fields and grow.

765
01:08:00,246 --> 01:08:04,925
Let's gather our strength
and then attack, Osman Bey.

766
01:08:07,726 --> 01:08:13,365
Whenever we wait, the infidels'
swords slit our throat, Hasan Bey.

767
01:08:13,606 --> 01:08:17,564
Waiting always gives courage to the infidel.

768
01:08:17,926 --> 01:08:22,045
Boran Bey is right, but...

769
01:08:22,446 --> 01:08:24,205
What if..

770
01:08:24,486 --> 01:08:26,925
What if we lose?

771
01:08:27,606 --> 01:08:30,365
Then we will be devastated.

772
01:08:30,366 --> 01:08:34,404
The Beylics that want to replace
the Seljuks will have an opportunity.

773
01:08:34,645 --> 01:08:38,845
Therefore, as Hasan Bey said...

774
01:08:39,006 --> 01:08:41,365
...even if it's just precautionary...

775
01:08:41,725 --> 01:08:44,205
...I also think waiting is
the right choice, my Bey.

776
01:08:44,206 --> 01:08:51,725
Courage is needed against the oppressor,
and freedom is needed against slavery, Beys.

777
01:08:52,566 --> 01:08:57,205
Those who are afraid of dying will die!

778
01:08:59,126 --> 01:09:04,604
I say we should not stop but continue, my Bey.

779
01:09:06,886 --> 01:09:09,085
What do you think we should do, Alaeddin?

780
01:09:10,326 --> 01:09:12,805
I am considering...

781
01:09:13,326 --> 01:09:16,045
...the strength of the army
as much as the war, my Bey.

782
01:09:16,046 --> 01:09:18,484
If the army weakens..

783
01:09:19,086 --> 01:09:21,885
...the state's survival will be in danger.

784
01:09:22,765 --> 01:09:25,885
Do you suggest we hold back from war?
-No, never.

785
01:09:26,126 --> 01:09:31,365
But I think it is wise to be cautious, my Bey.

786
01:09:36,046 --> 01:09:37,765
My Beys.

787
01:09:37,926 --> 01:09:39,805
My companions.

788
01:09:41,126 --> 01:09:43,205
I listened to you.

789
01:09:45,006 --> 01:09:47,885
Being a state according
to the Oghuz tradition...

790
01:09:47,886 --> 01:09:51,524
...is only possible with wise Beys like you.

791
01:09:52,606 --> 01:09:55,005
I understand your troubles.

792
01:09:55,246 --> 01:09:57,285
But know this..

793
01:09:57,286 --> 01:10:05,005
As long as we are on the right
path, Allah will always be with us.

794
01:10:05,006 --> 01:10:08,085
God willing, my Bey.

795
01:10:08,566 --> 01:10:15,885
Karesi, Candar, Germiyan, Karaman..

796
01:10:16,446 --> 01:10:18,685
...and all the other Beylics.

797
01:10:18,686 --> 01:10:20,405
All of them..

798
01:10:21,526 --> 01:10:24,885
All of them are trying to be like the Seljuks.

799
01:10:25,606 --> 01:10:27,245
We...

800
01:10:27,246 --> 01:10:29,765
...turn towards conquests...

801
01:10:29,766 --> 01:10:32,045
...instead of turning to their side..

802
01:10:32,046 --> 01:10:34,685
...we will gather many nomads whose hearts...

803
01:10:34,766 --> 01:10:38,005
...burn for war on our lands.

804
01:10:38,046 --> 01:10:38,965
Therefore...

805
01:10:38,966 --> 01:10:39,765
Therefore..

806
01:10:39,766 --> 01:10:42,165
...we will become stronger...

807
01:10:42,166 --> 01:10:44,565
...and our state will become stronger.

808
01:10:52,886 --> 01:10:58,205
All of you have the honor to
serve the great Roman ideal.

809
01:10:58,526 --> 01:11:02,885
You will do the necessary
and protect what is ours.

810
01:11:03,606 --> 01:11:06,245
-Right, Claudius?
-Yes, sir.

811
01:11:07,526 --> 01:11:12,805
While Turks are fighting each
other for the throne left from Seljuks,

812
01:11:13,446 --> 01:11:17,365
...we should reinforce our existence here.

813
01:11:20,206 --> 01:11:22,565
The biggest obstacle against us is Osman.

814
01:11:23,566 --> 01:11:27,525
Instead of fighting Turks and losing power.

815
01:11:27,966 --> 01:11:32,485
...Osman turned to us,
Byzantine, with all his strength.

816
01:11:34,526 --> 01:11:37,405
We need to find out what he plans,

817
01:11:38,006 --> 01:11:42,325
...understand his policy and make use of it.

818
01:11:43,806 --> 01:11:45,565
I agree.

819
01:11:45,686 --> 01:11:50,205
Yet Osman killed Orlok Kucar
and gained great reputation.

820
01:11:50,366 --> 01:11:52,565
The news spread all around.

821
01:11:53,246 --> 01:11:55,005
I agree with Lord Valens.

822
01:11:55,406 --> 01:12:01,245
He will lead all the Turkish Beys who avoid
the race of being the new Seljuk State.

823
01:12:01,646 --> 01:12:04,645
We hear Osman's name too much in Mudurnu.

824
01:12:05,086 --> 01:12:06,725
For this reason exactly.

825
01:12:07,246 --> 01:12:11,628
...we will gather under
the command of our great

826
01:12:11,640 --> 01:12:15,765
emperor and wipe Osman's
name off these lands.

827
01:12:16,326 --> 01:12:20,925
After every trouble, a great reward is offered.

828
01:12:21,766 --> 01:12:24,525
As long as we continue conquering.

829
01:12:24,846 --> 01:12:29,045
...we will make those nomad
settle in the places we conquer.

830
01:12:29,406 --> 01:12:32,525
So we will give the oppressed hope.

831
01:12:33,446 --> 01:12:39,725
Just then we will be the soldiers of
Turks in the plains of Anatolia, Osman Bey.

832
01:12:39,886 --> 01:12:41,525
God willing, my Bey!

833
01:12:41,526 --> 01:12:43,645
-God willing.
-God willing.

834
01:12:43,806 --> 01:12:45,485
God willing, God willing.

835
01:12:47,366 --> 01:12:49,285
Well said, my Bey.

836
01:12:50,566 --> 01:12:52,685
What is our target?

837
01:13:03,086 --> 01:13:04,685
Our target...

838
01:13:24,686 --> 01:13:26,405
Our target...

839
01:13:28,246 --> 01:13:30,445
..is the northern border.

840
01:13:32,126 --> 01:13:33,445
Here.

841
01:13:34,006 --> 01:13:37,525
Sakarya, Mudurnu, Goynuk.

842
01:13:38,446 --> 01:13:42,045
We will turn to those places.

843
01:13:42,286 --> 01:13:46,965
And we will have raids on them all the time.

844
01:13:48,486 --> 01:13:53,605
All of them are fertile
and watery lands, my Bey.

845
01:13:54,966 --> 01:13:57,285
They will make us stronger.

846
01:14:00,566 --> 01:14:02,765
How will we move our army, my Bey?

847
01:14:02,926 --> 01:14:06,645
Spies of the heathens are
wandering in all the borders.

848
01:14:07,366 --> 01:14:09,405
We will move our army...

849
01:14:11,166 --> 01:14:15,205
...through the hidden valleys in the west.

850
01:14:16,286 --> 01:14:17,765
For this reason,

851
01:14:18,646 --> 01:14:22,045
...everybody should prepare
their alps for these raids.

852
01:14:22,566 --> 01:14:28,285
In two days, we will meet in
Karacam and join together.

853
01:14:28,486 --> 01:14:31,045
As you order, my Bey!

854
01:14:32,486 --> 01:14:34,485
The council is over.

855
01:14:35,006 --> 01:14:38,285
We perform raid, Allah offers victory.

856
01:14:38,326 --> 01:14:40,725
-Aameen!
-Aameen, my Bey!

857
01:14:49,526 --> 01:14:52,085
As you all see,

858
01:14:52,326 --> 01:14:54,925
...the number of his followers is increasing.

859
01:14:55,126 --> 01:14:57,205
His army is growing bigger.

860
01:14:57,886 --> 01:15:01,125
Osman has had an important council today.

861
01:15:01,766 --> 01:15:03,685
He gathered all the Beys.

862
01:15:03,766 --> 01:15:09,845
Claudius and Sofia are supposed to
find out Osman's move after the council...

863
01:15:10,886 --> 01:15:13,365
...and stop him.

864
01:15:34,006 --> 01:15:38,525
And you should tighten the
security measures in your cities.

865
01:15:40,326 --> 01:15:43,205
You should reinforce your armies.

866
01:15:44,486 --> 01:15:47,365
You should organize your people.

867
01:15:47,726 --> 01:15:52,005
In this war, everybody will be a soldier.

868
01:15:52,206 --> 01:15:54,685
-As you wish.
-As you wish.

869
01:15:55,246 --> 01:16:01,205
Osman must learn a bitter lesson
that he shouldn't touch what is ours.

870
01:16:03,286 --> 01:16:08,125
The Byzantine fire that we
have raised will burn Osman first.

871
01:16:20,566 --> 01:16:24,365
While migrating, we almost ran out of gold.

872
01:16:24,966 --> 01:16:28,685
With this raid, we will gain some.

873
01:16:28,846 --> 01:16:31,365
It will be a cure for our trouble, God willing.

874
01:16:31,966 --> 01:16:34,365
-God willing.
-God willing.

875
01:16:34,446 --> 01:16:37,565
Fighters practiced with Mongolians.

876
01:16:38,086 --> 01:16:43,085
Now they will hit the Byzantine
borders like thunderbolts!

877
01:16:47,806 --> 01:16:49,365
-My man. -Brother.

878
01:16:49,486 --> 01:16:50,925
Gather the alps.

879
01:16:51,486 --> 01:16:55,605
We will be a sword for the
state and the cure for people.

880
01:16:58,046 --> 01:16:59,845
God willing, brother.

881
01:17:21,646 --> 01:17:23,085
Seyit.

882
01:17:31,086 --> 01:17:33,125
Listen to me carefully.

883
01:17:33,886 --> 01:17:36,925
Hear my words and tell Claudius...

884
01:17:37,126 --> 01:17:39,605
...about them one by one.

885
01:17:43,526 --> 01:17:45,325
Let's talk somewhere safer.

886
01:19:38,926 --> 01:19:40,685
Peace be upon you.

887
01:19:40,886 --> 01:19:42,965
-Peace be upon you too.
-Peace be upon you too.

888
01:19:46,166 --> 01:19:51,965
I'm ready with my five thousand
war-loving alps, Osman Bey.

889
01:19:53,086 --> 01:19:55,931
For the raid, I'm ready
with my three thousand alps

890
01:19:55,943 --> 01:19:58,525
who have wild horses
running inside, Osman Bey.

891
01:19:58,886 --> 01:20:01,125
Thank you, thank you.

892
01:20:03,726 --> 01:20:07,885
We destroyed the cruel ones one by
one who wanted to invade the Muslim lands.

893
01:20:10,566 --> 01:20:14,845
...we will stick our swords
of justice into their chests.

894
01:20:18,126 --> 01:20:21,085
Our people will share the booties.

895
01:20:21,726 --> 01:20:25,805
We'll always be under the
command of Islam banner.

896
01:20:27,006 --> 01:20:30,805
May The Creator bless our struggle..

897
01:20:31,006 --> 01:20:33,045
-Aameen.
-Aameen.

898
01:20:34,046 --> 01:20:35,445
Here we go.

899
01:21:11,526 --> 01:21:15,245
Osman's army will be here soon.

900
01:21:16,126 --> 01:21:22,525
My arches will shoot their arrows on
Osman's army like a storm with my call.

901
01:21:23,286 --> 01:21:27,765
When archers are done, the
infantry will come out of their covers...

902
01:21:28,046 --> 01:21:31,205
...and kill the rest of his army.

903
01:21:34,406 --> 01:21:39,805
Osman, you are going to
die with your army here today.

904
01:22:18,006 --> 01:22:21,205
Why did we stop, my Bey? Did you see something?

905
01:22:23,766 --> 01:22:27,085
Just stop, Koca Bey. Just stop.

906
01:22:40,246 --> 01:22:42,165
What is the news, Kanyumaz?

907
01:22:42,486 --> 01:22:46,565
My Bey, I checked all the
ways in the east as you ordered.

908
01:22:46,966 --> 01:22:50,245
The ways are safe and available
for our army to move through.

909
01:22:50,606 --> 01:22:52,085
There is nobody.

910
01:22:52,246 --> 01:22:53,445
Okay.

911
01:22:53,846 --> 01:22:57,565
In the council, you said
we would ride in the west.

912
01:22:57,846 --> 01:22:59,245
Didn't you, Osman Bey?

913
01:22:59,526 --> 01:23:01,925
Are we changing our route?

914
01:23:02,566 --> 01:23:04,125
Precautions, Koca Bey.

915
01:23:04,806 --> 01:23:06,245
Precautions.

916
01:23:08,006 --> 01:23:10,685
We take precautions, Allah offers victory.

917
01:23:11,006 --> 01:23:15,445
As long as the target is clear,
we can follow every path, my Bey.

918
01:23:15,566 --> 01:23:17,685
Alright. Here we go.

919
01:23:17,966 --> 01:23:21,285
-We'll ride to the east. Let's go.
-Come on.

920
01:23:32,606 --> 01:23:35,685
Let me see.

921
01:23:42,526 --> 01:23:43,245
Sister.

922
01:23:44,046 --> 01:23:46,365
The man you called insane.

923
01:23:49,646 --> 01:23:52,685
-Yes?
-He's been looking here.

924
01:23:53,606 --> 01:23:56,445
Ghazi told me...
-Halime!

925
01:23:58,926 --> 01:24:00,325
Fine.

926
01:24:00,486 --> 01:24:02,205
I didn't say anything.

927
01:24:05,766 --> 01:24:09,445
Why is that insane boy coming here?

928
01:24:18,566 --> 01:24:23,285
Bala Hatun, I want to help
with something if you let me.

929
01:24:23,766 --> 01:24:25,645
You are Koca Bey's son, right?

930
01:24:25,806 --> 01:24:28,765
Yes, my name is Oghuz. I'm at your service.

931
01:24:29,046 --> 01:24:30,525
Thanks, Oghuz.

932
01:24:30,606 --> 01:24:32,045
Stand ready then.

933
01:24:32,166 --> 01:24:35,925
We'll send the carts when we get
the news about Osman Bey's victory.

934
01:24:39,966 --> 01:24:41,565
I'm always ready.

935
01:24:47,206 --> 01:24:48,565
Bala Hatun.

936
01:24:49,526 --> 01:24:51,045
Sofia is here.

937
01:24:53,806 --> 01:24:56,045
She wants to see Halime Hatun.

938
01:24:57,766 --> 01:25:00,325
How dare she come here?

939
01:25:47,486 --> 01:25:50,005
Peace be upon you, Turgut Ghazi.

940
01:25:50,166 --> 01:25:51,445
Peace be upon you too.

941
01:25:51,566 --> 01:25:55,165
They call me Solgur Agha, the lion hunter.

942
01:25:55,686 --> 01:25:58,165
Welcome, Solgur Agha. Alright.

943
01:25:58,406 --> 01:25:59,445
Alright.

944
01:25:59,646 --> 01:26:02,925
We called you and you came instantly. Thank you.

945
01:26:03,086 --> 01:26:09,965
My brothers who would die for
our cause, with Osman Bey's order,

946
01:26:10,566 --> 01:26:13,165
...and I hunt heathens in the frontiers.

947
01:26:14,406 --> 01:26:19,085
I've heard that Osman Bey is having a raid.

948
01:26:19,286 --> 01:26:21,405
You heard right, Solgur Agha.

949
01:26:22,086 --> 01:26:25,205
That's why I gathered you here.

950
01:26:26,006 --> 01:26:32,925
I want to swing the glorious sword
of Turks in the front all together.

951
01:26:33,606 --> 01:26:36,325
We should be an example to young alps.

952
01:26:37,646 --> 01:26:39,845
I don't want them to die.

953
01:26:40,166 --> 01:26:42,485
What do you think history is?

954
01:26:43,166 --> 01:26:45,845
Mad men make history!

955
01:26:46,526 --> 01:26:48,925
We are the maddest!

956
01:26:49,246 --> 01:26:51,285
We only come around in the grave!

957
01:26:51,406 --> 01:26:54,405
We shall die if we have
to die and become martyrs!

958
01:26:54,646 --> 01:26:57,405
We'd gladly die for the Islam world!

959
01:26:57,566 --> 01:27:01,885
For the Islam world!
For the Islam world!

960
01:27:02,566 --> 01:27:05,605
Praise be, brave fighters.

961
01:27:05,886 --> 01:27:07,125
Praise be.

962
01:27:07,246 --> 01:27:11,165
What are these furs for, Turgut Ghazi?

963
01:27:11,926 --> 01:27:16,685
Our glorious horseshoes always
scared the enemy from the distance.

964
01:27:16,806 --> 01:27:22,965
These furs will make the hearts of
heathens shake with fear, for sure.

965
01:27:23,086 --> 01:27:24,445
God willing.

966
01:27:24,806 --> 01:27:26,005
God willing.

967
01:27:56,726 --> 01:27:58,885
Long live, Turgut Ghazi.

968
01:27:58,966 --> 01:28:00,085
Thank you.

969
01:28:00,406 --> 01:28:04,605
Let's go join the raid and
slaughter the heathens!

970
01:28:04,726 --> 01:28:06,205
Allah is the greatest!

971
01:28:06,286 --> 01:28:12,685
Allah is the greatest! Allah is the greatest!
Allah is the greatest! Allah is the greatest!

972
01:28:42,486 --> 01:28:43,845
Bala.

973
01:28:45,726 --> 01:28:49,165
That we let you live doesn't
mean you can come here freely.

974
01:28:49,486 --> 01:28:51,405
Don't push my patience.

975
01:28:51,606 --> 01:28:53,805
We aren't enemies anymore.

976
01:28:56,286 --> 01:28:58,045
I wanted to see Poena.

977
01:28:59,486 --> 01:29:02,245
My little bird, are you alright?

978
01:29:06,326 --> 01:29:07,645
I'm fine.

979
01:29:08,526 --> 01:29:10,085
You?

980
01:29:11,646 --> 01:29:12,925
I'm fine.

981
01:29:14,646 --> 01:29:18,045
I might be better if were with me, though.

982
01:29:18,446 --> 01:29:21,125
How is your disease?

983
01:29:23,646 --> 01:29:24,845
Fine.

984
01:29:25,846 --> 01:29:29,045
You said you were sick and would die.

985
01:29:30,286 --> 01:29:33,045
I asked the healer hatuns
who cured your sickness.

986
01:29:34,526 --> 01:29:38,205
You have no disease, Sofia.

987
01:29:40,286 --> 01:29:42,125
You lied again.

988
01:29:43,286 --> 01:29:44,645
You lied again.

989
01:29:44,926 --> 01:29:48,685
-Poena, I just...
-Wait, mother.

990
01:29:53,246 --> 01:29:55,725
My name is Halime.

991
01:29:56,446 --> 01:30:00,285
And if you come to see me again

992
01:30:01,046 --> 01:30:04,645
...I will kill you with my own hands.

993
01:30:21,326 --> 01:30:23,845
You heard what you needed to hear Sofia.

994
01:30:23,846 --> 01:30:25,685
Go now.

995
01:30:27,366 --> 01:30:29,045
Alps!

996
01:30:29,206 --> 01:30:32,365
Accompany Sofia on the way back.

997
01:30:44,166 --> 01:30:47,125
The carts will set out when
Osman Bey sends word.

998
01:30:47,126 --> 01:30:50,325
Until then, let's do our best, sister.

999
01:30:55,006 --> 01:30:57,205
Right, Bala.

1000
01:30:58,046 --> 01:31:01,525
I heard what I needed to hear.

1001
01:31:21,246 --> 01:31:22,685
Sir.

1002
01:31:22,686 --> 01:31:26,565
Osman will not march to the west,
he will march north with his army.

1003
01:31:26,566 --> 01:31:28,365
What do you mean north?

1004
01:31:28,366 --> 01:31:29,925
What are you saying?

1005
01:31:29,926 --> 01:31:31,805
Why would he turn from his path?

1006
01:31:31,806 --> 01:31:33,925
I don't know, sir.

1007
01:31:35,366 --> 01:31:37,405
Osman.

1008
01:31:37,966 --> 01:31:40,365
Where is his target?

1009
01:31:40,886 --> 01:31:43,405
Where will you attack?

1010
01:31:44,206 --> 01:31:46,165
Where will this shepherd attack?

1011
01:31:46,166 --> 01:31:47,165
Did he tell them?

1012
01:31:47,166 --> 01:31:49,805
I only know that they are heading north, sir.

1013
01:31:49,806 --> 01:31:52,445
Then, we will go north.

1014
01:31:52,646 --> 01:31:54,685
They are far ahead of you, sir.

1015
01:31:54,686 --> 01:31:59,605
Even if your horses die, you will not stop.

1016
01:31:59,966 --> 01:32:05,125
Osman will not reach his
target, wherever he goes.

1017
01:32:19,166 --> 01:32:20,885
Well done, Koca Bey.

1018
01:32:20,886 --> 01:32:24,605
Thank you, thank you Alaeddin.

1019
01:32:29,446 --> 01:32:34,285
There is no other nation as happy
as us before a war, thanks to Allah.

1020
01:32:34,766 --> 01:32:38,845
The battle is a celebration for
the Turks, Shahzade Alaeddin.

1021
01:32:38,846 --> 01:32:40,565
Right. Right.

1022
01:32:40,566 --> 01:32:43,205
Celebration for us, death for infidels.

1023
01:32:43,206 --> 01:32:45,005
You are right!

1024
01:32:45,006 --> 01:32:49,085
The sound of your sword
fills my heart with light.

1025
01:32:49,086 --> 01:32:51,525
My companion is my sword...

1026
01:32:51,606 --> 01:32:53,565
...my way is conquest...

1027
01:32:53,566 --> 01:32:55,285
...and my celebration is shahada.

1028
01:32:55,286 --> 01:32:57,645
May your life be long, Hasan brother.

1029
01:32:57,646 --> 01:32:59,045
Praise be. -Live long.

1030
01:32:59,086 --> 01:33:01,165
Thank you Koca Bey.

1031
01:33:01,166 --> 01:33:02,965
Thank you.

1032
01:33:04,206 --> 01:33:06,085
My Bey is coming.

1033
01:33:08,526 --> 01:33:09,725
Peace be upon you.

1034
01:33:09,726 --> 01:33:11,205
Peace be upon you too.

1035
01:33:11,705 --> 01:33:14,465
Peace be upon you too.

1036
01:33:16,286 --> 01:33:17,765
We will conquer Goynuk...

1037
01:33:17,766 --> 01:33:22,205
...with our swords and rule with justice.

1038
01:33:22,206 --> 01:33:24,245
We will keep conquering lands.

1039
01:33:24,246 --> 01:33:31,325
And we will take our children's dreams far away
with Beys who see shahada as a celebration.

1040
01:33:31,566 --> 01:33:33,725
The time has come.

1041
01:33:33,726 --> 01:33:38,285
Now we will strike the infidels like a spear.

1042
01:33:38,286 --> 01:33:41,645
God willing

1043
01:33:56,566 --> 01:33:59,285
Come! Listen to me!

1044
01:33:59,286 --> 01:34:00,765
Walk!

1045
01:34:00,766 --> 01:34:02,725
Do not forget!

1046
01:34:02,846 --> 01:34:05,005
Come!

1047
01:34:05,006 --> 01:34:08,165
Dear Romans!

1048
01:34:08,686 --> 01:34:14,285
Do not forget the orders of God!

1049
01:34:14,286 --> 01:34:15,925
Get closer to God!

1050
01:34:15,926 --> 01:34:18,405
Come here!

1051
01:34:19,566 --> 01:34:20,885
Stupid kid.

1052
01:34:20,886 --> 01:34:24,605
Forgive me sir.

1053
01:34:24,606 --> 01:34:26,205
Take this.

1054
01:34:27,446 --> 01:34:30,045
Increase the number of guards.

1055
01:34:30,526 --> 01:34:33,445
Claudius will attack Osman's army.

1056
01:34:33,446 --> 01:34:36,645
But we still need to be careful.

1057
01:34:43,726 --> 01:34:45,685
Father, let's sell these.

1058
01:34:45,686 --> 01:34:47,125
No, my daughter. I cannot.

1059
01:34:47,126 --> 01:34:49,645
I bought these because you were sick.

1060
01:34:49,646 --> 01:34:52,845
You need to eat these to get stronger.

1061
01:34:53,046 --> 01:34:55,005
They are here, sir.

1062
01:35:00,406 --> 01:35:03,565
By selling these goods at my
market, you are insulting me.

1063
01:35:03,606 --> 01:35:06,645
Forgive me, I couldn't work
because my daughter was ill.

1064
01:35:06,646 --> 01:35:08,125
Your daughter concerns you.

1065
01:35:08,126 --> 01:35:09,325
The marketplace concerns me.

1066
01:35:09,326 --> 01:35:10,885
Throw this man out of my marketplace.

1067
01:35:10,886 --> 01:35:13,365
Sir, forgive me! My family needs food!

1068
01:35:13,366 --> 01:35:15,805
I need to work, otherwise what will they eat?

1069
01:35:15,806 --> 01:35:17,885
Forgive me, sir.

1070
01:35:18,926 --> 01:35:19,885
Sir, forgive me!

1071
01:35:19,886 --> 01:35:20,525
Take him!

1072
01:35:20,526 --> 01:35:21,365
Father.

1073
01:35:21,366 --> 01:35:23,165
Don't be afraid, my daughter.

1074
01:35:23,166 --> 01:35:25,165
Sir, forgive me.

1075
01:35:25,206 --> 01:35:25,965
Sir...

1076
01:35:25,966 --> 01:35:28,885
Don't be afraid, my daughter.

1077
01:35:37,326 --> 01:35:39,645
A small price for the stall.

1078
01:35:39,646 --> 01:35:41,805
You can do business in my marketplace.

1079
01:35:41,806 --> 01:35:44,045
The stall is now yours.

1080
01:35:52,606 --> 01:35:54,925
My little bird..

1081
01:35:55,486 --> 01:35:59,085
...is threatening me with death, Hristo.

1082
01:35:59,446 --> 01:36:01,525
She is Turk, Sofia.

1083
01:36:01,526 --> 01:36:02,685
I raised her!

1084
01:36:02,686 --> 01:36:04,165
Like a Christian!

1085
01:36:05,446 --> 01:36:07,205
I raised her like my daughter.

1086
01:36:07,206 --> 01:36:10,325
And you will send the family
she chose over you to hell.

1087
01:36:10,326 --> 01:36:12,005
Claudius..

1088
01:36:12,006 --> 01:36:15,805
...will destroy Osman's dream of conquests.

1089
01:36:15,806 --> 01:36:20,245
We will also prevent aid
from going from the tribe.

1090
01:36:20,406 --> 01:36:22,005
Bala..

1091
01:36:22,006 --> 01:36:25,845
...has already prepared carts
full of ammunition and provisions.

1092
01:36:25,846 --> 01:36:29,125
Is it clear when the carts will set out?

1093
01:36:29,126 --> 01:36:33,725
After Claudius' move, they will ask for help.

1094
01:36:33,726 --> 01:36:36,565
We will be near the tribe.

1095
01:36:36,606 --> 01:36:38,765
Get ready.

1096
01:36:39,646 --> 01:36:41,805
We will raid...

1097
01:36:43,366 --> 01:36:45,605
...that caravan.

1098
01:36:48,606 --> 01:36:50,765
Come and get some!

1099
01:36:50,926 --> 01:36:54,245
Why do you think so?

1100
01:36:59,486 --> 01:37:04,085
Lord Valens!

1101
01:37:04,086 --> 01:37:06,445
Turks are coming!

1102
01:37:08,206 --> 01:37:09,405
Damn it!

1103
01:37:09,406 --> 01:37:11,405
Close the doors!

1104
01:37:13,606 --> 01:37:18,285
Do not touch their sacred
places, temples and churches!

1105
01:37:20,966 --> 01:37:23,285
Inform Claudius!

1106
01:37:25,326 --> 01:37:27,125
Attack!

1107
01:37:51,406 --> 01:37:54,085
Come on!

1108
01:37:58,566 --> 01:38:00,085
Come on

1109
01:38:18,406 --> 01:38:20,405
Damn it.

1110
01:38:21,326 --> 01:38:24,085
So your target was Goynuk, Osman.

1111
01:39:40,806 --> 01:39:43,885
Allah is the Greatest!

1112
01:39:50,046 --> 01:39:52,085
Goynuk will be your grave, Osman.

1113
01:39:52,086 --> 01:39:54,365
Come. Come here.

1114
01:39:59,966 --> 01:40:02,765
Lord Valens... or whatever you are called.

1115
01:40:04,246 --> 01:40:07,125
You won't even have a grave.

1116
01:40:07,206 --> 01:40:10,125
Your dead body will just decay.

1117
01:40:10,126 --> 01:40:11,725
Your time has come.

1118
01:40:11,726 --> 01:40:13,285
You can kill me.

1119
01:40:13,286 --> 01:40:16,445
But Claudius will not let you get away with it.

1120
01:40:17,606 --> 01:40:20,965
You will go to hell with Claudius.

1121
01:40:47,526 --> 01:40:49,685
Get rid of his dead body.

1122
01:41:18,646 --> 01:41:19,765
Tell me.

1123
01:41:19,766 --> 01:41:23,165
Osman... Osman conquered Goynuk, sir.

1124
01:41:23,966 --> 01:41:26,045
Damn it.

1125
01:41:26,446 --> 01:41:28,605
Are we going back, sir?

1126
01:41:29,926 --> 01:41:31,525
No.

1127
01:41:31,966 --> 01:41:34,085
We'll wait here.

1128
01:41:34,366 --> 01:41:37,405
We will let him think he gained a victory.

1129
01:41:37,686 --> 01:41:40,925
I will give him a defeat he will never forget.

1130
01:41:42,046 --> 01:41:44,245
Osman.

1131
01:41:56,486 --> 01:42:00,845
Don't be scared.

1132
01:42:01,326 --> 01:42:03,325
Don't be afraid.

1133
01:42:04,166 --> 01:42:05,965
Don t be scared.

1134
01:42:10,006 --> 01:42:12,365
Don't be scared.

1135
01:42:12,366 --> 01:42:17,125
We brought justice to Goynuk, not death.

1136
01:42:18,246 --> 01:42:23,445
Your goods, your lives, your honour...

1137
01:42:24,206 --> 01:42:26,445
...are entrusted to me.

1138
01:42:27,886 --> 01:42:30,645
Against all kinds of harm....

1139
01:42:31,526 --> 01:42:34,285
...my word will be a shield.

1140
01:42:35,886 --> 01:42:40,005
Don't... You were not defeated.

1141
01:42:40,806 --> 01:42:45,325
Hope and salvation rose like the sun in Goynuk.

1142
01:42:45,326 --> 01:42:51,445
Thank you Osman Bey.

1143
01:42:53,246 --> 01:42:55,245
Alps, search the houses!

1144
01:42:55,286 --> 01:42:57,765
Check if there are soldiers who are hiding!

1145
01:42:57,766 --> 01:43:02,725
As you order, my Bey.

1146
01:43:03,606 --> 01:43:05,525
Kanyumaz.

1147
01:43:06,486 --> 01:43:08,845
Place guards on the walls.

1148
01:43:09,286 --> 01:43:11,965
Goynuk is now the property of Kayi.

1149
01:43:19,166 --> 01:43:22,045
Let our banner wave on the walls.

1150
01:43:23,966 --> 01:43:25,565
Alright brother.

1151
01:43:25,566 --> 01:43:30,245
Osman Bey's banner will give fear to
the infidels and hope to the oppressed.

1152
01:43:30,246 --> 01:43:31,965
Hay Praise be!

1153
01:43:31,966 --> 01:43:33,965
Praise be!

1154
01:43:34,006 --> 01:43:35,425
Come on Alps!

1155
01:43:35,425 --> 01:43:37,245
In the name of Allah!

1156
01:43:41,086 --> 01:43:43,325
Take them where the other prisoners are.

1157
01:43:51,526 --> 01:43:53,165
You stop

1158
01:43:53,886 --> 01:43:55,765
Let me look at you.

1159
01:44:00,726 --> 01:44:05,285
From now on, you will be with me.

1160
01:44:06,286 --> 01:44:09,405
Yigit Bey, what are you doing?

1161
01:44:10,086 --> 01:44:11,365
Hasan Bey.

1162
01:44:13,086 --> 01:44:15,245
I'm taking my share from the booty.

1163
01:44:16,566 --> 01:44:17,805
This woman..

1164
01:44:19,406 --> 01:44:21,685
...will be my odalisque.

1165
01:44:24,486 --> 01:44:27,805
You can't take anything
without Osman Bey's permission.

1166
01:44:27,806 --> 01:44:29,925
We need to consult Osman Bey first.

1167
01:44:30,086 --> 01:44:32,565
I'm leading a miserable life here.

1168
01:44:32,966 --> 01:44:37,765
I'll be happy to be the
odalisque of such a brave Bey.

1169
01:44:39,526 --> 01:44:40,925
You heard her.

1170
01:44:42,846 --> 01:44:46,085
-Give me patience, my Allah.
-Here we go.

1171
01:44:53,246 --> 01:44:54,485
-Alaeddin.
-My Bey.

1172
01:44:54,566 --> 01:44:57,325
Are there any Byzantine
soldiers left in the city?

1173
01:44:57,326 --> 01:44:59,245
Did you meet the needs of people?

1174
01:44:59,366 --> 01:45:00,645
The city is safe, my Bey.

1175
01:45:00,766 --> 01:45:03,005
People got fed, for sure.

1176
01:45:03,086 --> 01:45:04,045
Thank you.

1177
01:45:07,806 --> 01:45:10,605
My Bey, Turgut Ghazi is coming.

1178
01:45:27,686 --> 01:45:28,765
Peace be upon you.

1179
01:45:28,806 --> 01:45:30,805
Peace be upon you too.
Peace be upon you too.

1180
01:45:33,206 --> 01:45:35,285
May your conquest be blessed, Osman.

1181
01:45:35,406 --> 01:45:37,045
Thank you, Turgut Ghazi.

1182
01:45:37,126 --> 01:45:38,605
Thank you.

1183
01:45:40,086 --> 01:45:44,005
Well... The elders of my tribe.

1184
01:45:45,086 --> 01:45:46,765
Old wolves.

1185
01:45:46,926 --> 01:45:47,885
Welcome.

1186
01:45:47,926 --> 01:45:49,565
Thank you, Osman Bey.

1187
01:45:49,886 --> 01:45:51,405
Praise be, my Bey.

1188
01:45:51,726 --> 01:45:54,245
You look very well. Praise be.

1189
01:45:54,406 --> 01:45:55,765
Praise be.

1190
01:45:58,406 --> 01:46:02,965
Well, Solgur Agha. You carried
out your duty in the frontiers properly.

1191
01:46:03,766 --> 01:46:06,925
Now you will stand beside me.

1192
01:46:07,006 --> 01:46:14,205
I'd like to fight beside in the front with
Turgut Ghazi with your permission, my Bey.

1193
01:46:14,366 --> 01:46:18,605
We will put fear in hearts and
spread the glory of Turks in battlefields.

1194
01:46:18,726 --> 01:46:19,885
Surely.

1195
01:46:20,726 --> 01:46:21,645
Surely.

1196
01:46:21,766 --> 01:46:26,445
To let the young live longer, we
will sacrifice ourselves, Osman Bey.

1197
01:46:26,566 --> 01:46:27,925
Thank you.

1198
01:46:28,766 --> 01:46:33,005
Some old men are waiting
for death in their beds.

1199
01:46:33,366 --> 01:46:36,725
And some never avoid fights like you.

1200
01:46:38,486 --> 01:46:41,405
And this would only suit mad hearts. 
Long live everyone.

1201
01:46:41,406 --> 01:46:43,325
-Thank you, my Bey.
-Thank you,, my Bey.

1202
01:46:43,446 --> 01:46:48,405
We'll gladly sacrifice our lives
for the Islam cause, my Bey.

1203
01:46:49,926 --> 01:46:51,725
What is the target?

1204
01:46:52,286 --> 01:46:54,605
Tell us so we can leave in no time.

1205
01:46:58,326 --> 01:47:00,085
The target

1206
01:47:23,726 --> 01:47:27,605
Who is the impertinent man
who comes in without permission?

1207
01:47:33,886 --> 01:47:35,685
You betrayed me.

1208
01:47:36,726 --> 01:47:38,365
What are you doing here?

1209
01:47:39,886 --> 01:47:42,005
You're risking our lives.

1210
01:47:42,446 --> 01:47:44,405
I'm here to bring you to account.

1211
01:47:44,646 --> 01:47:47,165
Osman didn't use the route that you told me.

1212
01:47:47,366 --> 01:47:49,765
I lost Goynuk because of you.

1213
01:47:53,846 --> 01:47:56,125
Why would I do that?

1214
01:47:56,326 --> 01:47:58,765
Osman tricked all of

1215
01:47:58,806 --> 01:48:01,245
He changed the route in the last minute.

1216
01:48:01,526 --> 01:48:04,325
I had no time to inform you.

1217
01:48:05,486 --> 01:48:07,765
I'm telling the truth.

1218
01:48:09,966 --> 01:48:11,805
I lost Goynuk.

1219
01:48:12,606 --> 01:48:15,085
I won't lose any other lands.

1220
01:48:26,766 --> 01:48:28,645
Don't worry.

1221
01:48:29,406 --> 01:48:31,605
Osman will set the new target.

1222
01:48:32,686 --> 01:48:35,485
We will catch him this time.

1223
01:48:38,606 --> 01:48:40,685
He'll definitely fall into our trap.

1224
01:48:43,166 --> 01:48:44,805
You go now.

1225
01:48:45,006 --> 01:48:46,765
Don't be caught here.

1226
01:48:47,926 --> 01:48:49,285
Wait for my call.

1227
01:48:53,286 --> 01:48:58,725
Do not come to me false intelligence again!

1228
01:49:13,366 --> 01:49:14,285
Mother.

1229
01:49:14,326 --> 01:49:15,845
Yes, my dear?

1230
01:49:16,246 --> 01:49:19,165
My father and brothers are having raids.

1231
01:49:19,806 --> 01:49:21,725
But we just wait in the tribe.

1232
01:49:23,286 --> 01:49:24,885
Will it always be this way?

1233
01:49:25,086 --> 01:49:27,285
Well said, sister.

1234
01:49:27,846 --> 01:49:31,205
I always complain about this, but...

1235
01:49:31,766 --> 01:49:33,845
...nothing changes.

1236
01:49:34,166 --> 01:49:35,765
Oh no.

1237
01:49:36,646 --> 01:49:39,805
Your job got harder, mother.
You have to deal with two now.

1238
01:49:40,726 --> 01:49:41,925
Yes.

1239
01:49:42,886 --> 01:49:46,485
A conquest cannot be performed
only with swords, my dear.

1240
01:49:49,326 --> 01:49:50,805
How is it performed, mother?

1241
01:49:56,966 --> 01:49:58,645
Look at her!

1242
01:49:59,166 --> 01:50:02,845
She doesn't say she can't sew but keeps yawning.

1243
01:50:08,486 --> 01:50:11,645
Come here. Come closer.

1244
01:50:12,046 --> 01:50:15,885
Come. Come here.

1245
01:50:17,886 --> 01:50:20,245
My big babies.

1246
01:50:23,486 --> 01:50:28,205
Gonca, they both lie on my knees
and say they want to join raids. You see?

1247
01:50:28,446 --> 01:50:30,525
-I see.
-Mother.

1248
01:50:34,646 --> 01:50:37,605
They have a mother and she spoils them.

1249
01:50:39,606 --> 01:50:45,725
Well... Look at me. I can
spoil you too, my pretty girl.

1250
01:50:47,246 --> 01:50:51,085
Oh my sister-in-law.
Oh my sister-in-law...

1251
01:50:52,326 --> 01:50:56,365
Mother, you said a conquest
cannot be performed only with swords.

1252
01:50:56,926 --> 01:50:58,245
How is it performed?

1253
01:50:58,486 --> 01:51:00,605
Don't be jealous of my sister at least.

1254
01:51:02,486 --> 01:51:04,005
Fatma.

1255
01:51:06,006 --> 01:51:08,165
A land is conquered but...

1256
01:51:08,486 --> 01:51:13,365
...if a baby isn't born in that
land, you can't own that land.

1257
01:51:17,486 --> 01:51:21,805
Mother, we haven't got
any news about father yet.

1258
01:51:24,526 --> 01:51:26,725
What do you think they are doing?

1259
01:51:27,526 --> 01:51:31,405
Go perform your ablutions. Let's pray. Come on.

1260
01:51:34,126 --> 01:51:36,125
Do I have permission Bala Hatun?

1261
01:51:36,446 --> 01:51:38,005
Come in, Kismet.

1262
01:51:42,766 --> 01:51:44,685
Great news, Bala Hatun.

1263
01:51:45,046 --> 01:51:46,485
Kismet, did they?

1264
01:51:46,726 --> 01:51:48,685
Osman Bey conquered Goynuk.

1265
01:51:48,926 --> 01:51:51,645
Thanks to Allah.

1266
01:51:52,406 --> 01:51:53,485
Thanks to Allah.

1267
01:51:53,526 --> 01:51:55,325
Now we have to take action.

1268
01:51:55,366 --> 01:51:58,285
At dawn tomorrow, the
caravan will leave for Goynuk.

1269
01:51:58,486 --> 01:52:00,405
Finish the preparations.

1270
01:52:00,606 --> 01:52:03,165
-Come on, pack up.
-Alright.

1271
01:52:03,646 --> 01:52:04,965
Come on.

1272
01:52:06,446 --> 01:52:09,565
We distributed the booties
as you ordered, my Bey.

1273
01:52:09,846 --> 01:52:13,285
And we sent their shares
to the houses of our martyrs.

1274
01:52:14,966 --> 01:52:18,045
We will give everybody their shares.

1275
01:52:19,766 --> 01:52:23,765
Now it's time to encourage
the hearts for the new horizons.

1276
01:52:28,326 --> 01:52:33,045
What about the odalisques and
the prisoners we captured, my Bey?

1277
01:52:37,446 --> 01:52:41,565
We will inform them about Islam.

1278
01:52:42,566 --> 01:52:45,885
Whoever doesn't accept will pay the price.

1279
01:52:46,686 --> 01:52:49,525
Those who want to marry our alps can do it.

1280
01:52:50,406 --> 01:52:54,445
Those who don't want will be
assigned for duties with our sisters.

1281
01:52:56,326 --> 01:52:57,925
As you order, my Bey.

1282
01:53:06,166 --> 01:53:08,205
I've built up the fire of battle.

1283
01:53:09,046 --> 01:53:10,965
We can't stop now.

1284
01:53:11,406 --> 01:53:16,685
They can't stand against the
fate we draw with our swords.

1285
01:53:16,926 --> 01:53:19,965
-With Allah's will, my Bey.
-With Allah's will, my Bey.

1286
01:53:22,046 --> 01:53:24,245
When the target is set,

1287
01:53:25,206 --> 01:53:29,445
...we will put our iron fists on
the enemy's chest, for sure.

1288
01:53:29,686 --> 01:53:30,965
For sure.

1289
01:53:32,526 --> 01:53:36,325
Our target is Mudurnu.

1290
01:53:42,966 --> 01:53:47,165
The castle of Mudurnu both
stands on the trade route...

1291
01:53:47,766 --> 01:53:50,245
...and has very fertile lands, my Bey.

1292
01:53:51,766 --> 01:53:53,045
Koca Bey.

1293
01:53:53,166 --> 01:53:56,405
Prepare your alps tomorrow morning.

1294
01:53:56,486 --> 01:53:58,005
This duty is yours.

1295
01:53:58,566 --> 01:54:00,125
As you order, my Bey.

1296
01:54:01,566 --> 01:54:03,205
-Alaaddin.
-My Bey.

1297
01:54:03,406 --> 01:54:06,765
The catapults and the
battering rams to hit the walls.

1298
01:54:07,166 --> 01:54:08,685
This duty is yours.

1299
01:54:09,206 --> 01:54:10,445
As you order, my Bey.

1300
01:54:11,086 --> 01:54:13,285
Thank you, thank you.

1301
01:54:13,806 --> 01:54:19,925
And we will set out at the dawn.

1302
01:54:21,606 --> 01:54:26,565
We'll go through the hidden
valleys to reach Mudurnu.

1303
01:54:28,606 --> 01:54:34,445
Turgut Ghazi and Solgur
Agha. You will leave tonight.

1304
01:54:34,646 --> 01:54:37,205
You need to check all the way.

1305
01:54:38,206 --> 01:54:39,125
Alright.

1306
01:54:39,246 --> 01:54:41,285
As you order, my Bey.

1307
01:54:42,366 --> 01:54:45,445
Here we go. May our fight be blessed.

1308
01:54:45,766 --> 01:54:51,605
May Allah let us be
victorious, who follow Islam.

1309
01:54:51,966 --> 01:54:53,485
-Aameen.
-Aameen.

1310
01:54:53,806 --> 01:54:55,165
Aameen.

1311
01:55:09,766 --> 01:55:13,765
We placed all the healing materials, mother.

1312
01:55:14,726 --> 01:55:15,365
Fine.

1313
01:55:15,446 --> 01:55:18,525
Food, clothes, weapons.

1314
01:55:19,126 --> 01:55:21,645
We prepared everything, Bala Hatun.

1315
01:55:21,766 --> 01:55:23,125
Good. Praise be.

1316
01:55:23,126 --> 01:55:26,645
I'll keep watching the tribe with
Sisters and continue the preparations.

1317
01:55:26,646 --> 01:55:29,045
-You'll go to Goynuk.
-As you order, mother.

1318
01:55:29,206 --> 01:55:30,645
As you order, mother.

1319
01:55:31,046 --> 01:55:35,725
Cerkutay Bey, you will watch the carts to make
sure that they reach the army camp safely.

1320
01:55:35,966 --> 01:55:37,445
As you order, Bala Hatun.

1321
01:55:37,606 --> 01:55:41,885
Oghuz Bey and alps will accompany you.

1322
01:55:48,246 --> 01:55:50,325
Have a safe travel.

1323
01:55:50,806 --> 01:55:52,445
-Come on.
-Come on, alps!

1324
01:55:52,686 --> 01:55:54,245
We have a long way.

1325
01:56:09,406 --> 01:56:11,805
Mother, isn't Halime going?

1326
01:56:12,846 --> 01:56:15,405
I'm here!

1327
01:56:15,606 --> 01:56:18,205
I'm here.

1328
01:56:24,606 --> 01:56:27,205
I really have a lot to do with you...

1329
01:56:27,246 --> 01:56:29,565
I know you love me, sister.

1330
01:56:29,566 --> 01:56:31,565
I love you too.

1331
01:56:31,566 --> 01:56:33,965
Come on. Go now.

1332
01:56:33,966 --> 01:56:36,325
Come on! Come on.

1333
01:56:46,686 --> 01:56:50,245
Attention! Osman Bey!

1334
01:57:16,006 --> 01:57:21,085
My Beys. My Alps. We conquered Goynuk.

1335
01:57:21,286 --> 01:57:23,205
Now this place belongs to us.

1336
01:57:25,686 --> 01:57:28,965
Everyone must know.

1337
01:57:29,726 --> 01:57:31,885
Our target is Mudurnu.

1338
01:57:32,326 --> 01:57:34,765
They are all waiting for us.

1339
01:57:34,766 --> 01:57:37,005
Let them wait for us.

1340
01:57:37,006 --> 01:57:43,125
We will bring the justice of Islam
to Rome, where injustice rules.

1341
01:57:43,126 --> 01:57:44,925
God willing.

1342
01:57:45,526 --> 01:57:47,485
Allah is the Greatest!

1343
01:58:21,446 --> 01:58:23,965
Have the soldiers taken their positions?

1344
01:58:24,086 --> 01:58:25,125
They are all ready.

1345
01:58:25,126 --> 01:58:27,045
They are waiting for your orders.

1346
01:58:27,046 --> 01:58:28,725
Good.

1347
01:58:29,446 --> 01:58:31,485
Tell them.

1348
01:58:31,486 --> 01:58:35,525
Everyone in the caravan will die.

1349
01:58:43,086 --> 01:58:44,725
Fatma Hatun.

1350
01:58:44,726 --> 01:58:46,445
I am sorry.

1351
01:58:46,446 --> 01:58:47,925
What happened?

1352
01:58:47,926 --> 01:58:50,205
Are you starting to act smart?

1353
01:58:50,646 --> 01:58:52,765
I am asking for your forgiveness.

1354
01:58:52,766 --> 01:58:54,845
And you are still calling me a lunatic.

1355
01:58:54,846 --> 01:58:56,125
Why are you doing this?

1356
01:58:56,166 --> 01:58:58,685
Why are you asking for forgiveness?

1357
01:58:59,526 --> 01:59:02,565
I didn't know you were Osman Bey's daughter.

1358
01:59:03,646 --> 01:59:06,725
You treat people differently than.

1359
01:59:07,086 --> 01:59:09,405
What would you do if I were one of the people?

1360
01:59:09,406 --> 01:59:12,765
Would you still ask for forgiveness?

1361
01:59:12,766 --> 01:59:15,005
Or are you scared?

1362
01:59:15,006 --> 01:59:16,845
I don't know what fear is.

1363
01:59:16,846 --> 01:59:18,525
But I made a mistake.

1364
01:59:18,526 --> 01:59:20,485
You are seriously arrogant.

1365
01:59:20,486 --> 01:59:25,845
And you are a cowardly lunatic.

1366
01:59:42,766 --> 01:59:46,325
My Yigit Bey ordered me to give this to you.

1367
01:59:46,326 --> 01:59:47,925
Sir.

1368
01:59:55,926 --> 01:59:58,005
Tell Yigit Bey...

1369
01:59:58,006 --> 02:00:03,005
When this is over, he will be
rewarded for all the things he did.

1370
02:00:09,886 --> 02:00:13,165
So you will attack Mudurnu, Osman.

1371
02:00:14,326 --> 02:00:17,085
You will pass through narrow passages...

1372
02:00:17,126 --> 02:00:19,365
...for the Mudurnu castle.

1373
02:00:20,086 --> 02:00:23,245
Those narrow passages will become your grave.

1374
02:00:26,566 --> 02:00:28,925
Everyone get ready.

1375
02:00:29,526 --> 02:00:31,325
We are leaving.

1376
02:00:42,846 --> 02:00:44,685
Archers!

1377
02:00:47,246 --> 02:00:48,725
Ambush! Be careful

1378
02:00:48,766 --> 02:00:51,085
Be careful!

1379
02:00:51,086 --> 02:00:52,125
Behind the carts!

1380
02:00:52,126 --> 02:00:54,805
Come on! Come on! Fatma!

1381
02:01:10,366 --> 02:01:12,285
Come on.

1382
02:01:36,846 --> 02:01:38,725
It's Hristo.

1383
02:01:46,766 --> 02:01:48,565
Sofia

1384
02:01:48,566 --> 02:01:51,165
I will kill you all!

1385
02:01:51,166 --> 02:01:52,885
I will not let this happen!

1386
02:01:52,966 --> 02:01:54,805
Stop! Stop, sister.

1387
02:01:54,926 --> 02:01:58,765
Now she is our enemy.

1388
02:01:58,766 --> 02:02:00,725
Gonca Hatun.

1389
02:02:01,926 --> 02:02:03,685
You have the back side.

1390
02:02:03,686 --> 02:02:05,125
Attack.

1391
02:02:05,126 --> 02:02:06,765
I'll handle it.

1392
02:02:06,846 --> 02:02:10,005
Sisters, move to the back!

1393
02:02:10,006 --> 02:02:12,685
Alps! Come here! -Attack!

1394
02:02:12,686 --> 02:02:15,445
Come on

1395
02:03:06,166 --> 02:03:07,845
Sisters!

1396
02:03:07,846 --> 02:03:11,084
Every loaf of bread baked
in this oven gives strength

1397
02:03:11,096 --> 02:03:14,045
to our valiants who run
from one raid to another.

1398
02:03:14,966 --> 02:03:16,725
I know.

1399
02:03:18,286 --> 02:03:19,645
You are tired.

1400
02:03:19,646 --> 02:03:21,725
But be patient, alright?

1401
02:03:21,726 --> 02:03:23,405
Thank you, Bala Hatun.

1402
02:03:23,406 --> 02:03:25,805
May Allah bless you, Bala Hatun.

1403
02:03:25,806 --> 02:03:27,485
May Allah bless you too.

1404
02:03:27,486 --> 02:03:29,405
Bala Hatun!

1405
02:03:31,606 --> 02:03:33,405
Kismet!

1406
02:03:33,686 --> 02:03:36,605
The watcher Alps saw Byzantine soldiers nearby.

1407
02:03:36,606 --> 02:03:38,965
They followed. They are Sofia's soldiers.

1408
02:03:38,966 --> 02:03:39,925
Sofia?

1409
02:03:40,046 --> 02:03:41,605
Where were they going?

1410
02:03:41,606 --> 02:03:45,205
They were close to the road
to Akcatas Cave, Bala Hatun.

1411
02:03:49,526 --> 02:03:52,165
She wanted to make peace yesterday.

1412
02:03:52,166 --> 02:03:54,125
Sofia..

1413
02:03:54,126 --> 02:03:55,845
She will raid the carts..

1414
02:03:55,846 --> 02:03:58,005
...going to Goynuk, huh?

1415
02:03:58,006 --> 02:04:00,925
Sofia made peace, but...
The snake sheds its skin often...

1416
02:04:00,926 --> 02:04:03,045
...but its habit never changes Kismet.

1417
02:04:03,046 --> 02:04:06,045
Get ready, we are leaving!
Come on! Come on Kismet!

1418
02:04:12,886 --> 02:04:15,205
Come, Osman.

1419
02:04:15,566 --> 02:04:18,525
Mudurnu will become your grave.

1420
02:04:58,086 --> 02:05:00,085
Get off your horses.

1421
02:05:15,046 --> 02:05:17,365
You will burn, Osman!

1422
02:05:17,446 --> 02:05:21,885
With this fire, you and those
who believe in you will burn!

1423
02:05:21,886 --> 02:05:24,885
You will pay for what you did in Goynuk!

1424
02:05:25,166 --> 02:05:28,005
Are you going to scare us with fire, huh?

1425
02:05:28,766 --> 02:05:30,245
Alps, attack!

1426
02:05:30,246 --> 02:05:32,165
Attack!

1427
02:06:25,326 --> 02:06:26,965
Come on, Yigit brother!

1428
02:06:26,966 --> 02:06:30,245
Let's kill these infidels!

1429
02:06:33,166 --> 02:06:36,005
We will, brother, we will!

1430
02:07:04,606 --> 02:07:07,685
Come on valiants!

1431
02:07:30,086 --> 02:07:33,485
My Bey! They surrounded us, my Bey!

1432
02:07:35,206 --> 02:07:37,805
Hang on!

1433
02:07:39,446 --> 02:07:43,525
Come on brothers! Come on!

1434
02:07:44,566 --> 02:07:47,205
We melted the iron mountains!

1435
02:07:47,206 --> 02:07:48,725
What can they do to us, huh?

1436
02:07:48,726 --> 02:07:50,405
Attack!

1437
02:08:25,446 --> 02:08:29,365
Sofia!

1438
02:08:31,766 --> 02:08:35,005
I told you not to stand before me again.

1439
02:08:35,006 --> 02:08:37,285
Calm down, my little bird.

1440
02:08:44,246 --> 02:08:46,005
You lied again!

1441
02:08:46,006 --> 02:08:47,685
Poena.

1442
02:09:16,366 --> 02:09:19,605
This is me, Poena.

1443
02:09:19,606 --> 02:09:20,885
But this is not you!

1444
02:09:20,886 --> 02:09:24,165
I am suffering in pain
as I see you in this state!

1445
02:09:24,166 --> 02:09:25,565
Go to hell, Sofia.

1446
02:09:25,566 --> 02:09:26,805
Go to hell.

1447
02:09:26,806 --> 02:09:28,365
But I...

1448
02:09:28,366 --> 02:09:30,845
...for the first time in my life, I am in peace.

1449
02:09:30,846 --> 02:09:33,405
You have one last chance.

1450
02:09:33,406 --> 02:09:35,325
You will either come with me...

1451
02:09:35,326 --> 02:09:38,125
...or you will die like the rest of your family.

1452
02:09:38,126 --> 02:09:39,325
No.

1453
02:09:44,406 --> 02:09:49,365
Then you'll watch your sister die, Poena.

1454
02:09:50,246 --> 02:09:51,365
Kill Fatma!

1455
02:09:51,366 --> 02:09:53,325
No!

1456
02:09:54,006 --> 02:09:56,565
I won't let you hurt her!

1457
02:09:58,926 --> 02:10:01,045
You still don't understand Sofia.

1458
02:10:01,046 --> 02:10:04,165
You cannot scare us with death.

1459
02:10:15,086 --> 02:10:17,605
I am behind you, Bey's daughter.

1460
02:10:18,166 --> 02:10:20,445
I told you I did not know what fear was.

1461
02:10:20,446 --> 02:10:25,245
You were right. Surely, I will
return your favor, Bey's lunatic son.

1462
02:10:31,566 --> 02:10:33,685
You go, my Bey!

1463
02:10:33,726 --> 02:10:36,085
I will deal with the rest here!

1464
02:10:36,486 --> 02:10:38,925
Thank you Turhan!

1465
02:10:59,126 --> 02:11:02,485
My Bey, we are stuck here!

1466
02:11:07,486 --> 02:11:09,485
It's over Osman! It's over!

1467
02:11:09,486 --> 02:11:12,165
I extinguished your fire of conquest!

1468
02:11:12,166 --> 02:11:14,405
That was it!

1469
02:11:32,206 --> 02:11:34,045
We are here, my Osman!

1470
02:11:34,326 --> 02:11:37,085
Allah is the Greatest!

1471
02:11:41,326 --> 02:11:44,525
Allah is the Greatest!

1472
02:11:50,366 --> 02:11:52,845
Did you think we did not take precautions?

1473
02:11:52,846 --> 02:11:54,925
It's not over until I say it is.

1474
02:11:54,926 --> 02:11:56,165
Attack!

1475
02:12:28,726 --> 02:12:31,765
You arrived just in time, Turgut Ghazi.

1476
02:12:32,766 --> 02:12:35,645
I will be behind you as long as I live, Osman.

1477
02:12:39,846 --> 02:12:42,205
Let's kill all the infidels here!

1478
02:12:42,206 --> 02:12:44,565
Today we will forget our old age!

1479
02:13:22,206 --> 02:13:27,805
Allah is the Greatest!

1480
02:13:29,006 --> 02:13:31,885
We are retreating!

1481
02:13:31,886 --> 02:13:33,605
Osman, I will come!

1482
02:13:34,166 --> 02:13:36,645
I swear I will come for you!

1483
02:13:44,206 --> 02:13:45,605
You're running off, huh?

1484
02:13:45,886 --> 02:13:48,325
You can run off to the death only!

1485
02:13:48,806 --> 02:13:50,365
Go wherever you want.

1486
02:13:59,006 --> 02:14:00,365
My Bey.

1487
02:14:00,926 --> 02:14:04,005
Thankfully, Turgut Ghazi
and alps came to help in time.

1488
02:14:05,206 --> 02:14:06,725
For sure.

1489
02:14:06,806 --> 02:14:11,805
But the dog called Claudius...
How did he know about this route?

1490
02:14:22,126 --> 02:14:23,525
My Bey.

1491
02:14:25,606 --> 02:14:27,525
After Goynuk,

1492
02:14:27,926 --> 02:14:31,605
...they must have placed
watchmen all around with fear.

1493
02:14:31,686 --> 02:14:33,245
It doesn't matter.

1494
02:14:33,566 --> 02:14:35,445
We have only one target.

1495
02:14:35,886 --> 02:14:37,525
We'll capture Mudurnu.

1496
02:14:37,766 --> 02:14:42,245
Until we capture Mudurnu, our swords
will never go back in their sheathes.

1497
02:14:42,486 --> 02:14:45,125
-As you order, my Bey.
-As you order, my Bey.

1498
02:14:45,126 --> 02:14:46,285
As you order, my Bey.

1499
02:14:52,806 --> 02:14:54,805
I raised you.

1500
02:14:54,966 --> 02:14:58,005
You can't kill me until I want you to do so.

1501
02:15:29,366 --> 02:15:30,805
I am...

1502
02:15:31,606 --> 02:15:33,845
...the daughter of my mother and father.

1503
02:15:34,086 --> 02:15:36,645
Sofia, I'm Kayi.

1504
02:15:37,326 --> 02:15:40,965
You can no longer predict my next move.

1505
02:15:46,846 --> 02:15:48,605
Halime!

1506
02:15:51,166 --> 02:15:54,965
You killed my Poena.

1507
02:15:56,086 --> 02:15:58,165
I will kill you.

1508
02:16:01,086 --> 02:16:02,285
Halime!

1509
02:16:03,286 --> 02:16:04,965
Sofia!

1510
02:16:07,926 --> 02:16:10,605
-Mother.
-I will be your death!

1511
02:16:11,326 --> 02:16:12,965
Alps, Sisters.

1512
02:16:13,286 --> 02:16:17,845
Crush everyone who stands in your way
until Osman Bey's goods reach Goynuk.

1513
02:16:18,126 --> 02:16:19,805
Allah is the greatest!

1514
02:16:22,166 --> 02:16:26,485
Soldiers, let nobody survive!

1515
02:16:28,566 --> 02:16:31,365
Nobody.

1516
02:17:01,606 --> 02:17:03,843
I'm Osman Bey.

1517
02:17:04,846 --> 02:17:07,965
I have never abandoned the right path.

1518
02:17:09,004 --> 02:17:12,245
I have never give up on the cause of Turks.

1519
02:17:13,566 --> 02:17:17,965
I have never bowed to anyone
to raise just a little higher.

1520
02:17:19,924 --> 02:17:23,965
I've made my father's beylic grow
bigger and develop into a state.

1521
02:17:26,726 --> 02:17:29,365
I've stood against the cruel.

1522
02:17:30,606 --> 02:17:32,763
I've helped the oppressed.

1523
02:17:35,004 --> 02:17:37,885
In this path, death is martyrdom to me.

1524
02:17:39,084 --> 02:17:41,485
Now I'm telling my nation...

1525
02:17:42,566 --> 02:17:46,004
Either we will fight the pharaohs and vanish...

1526
02:17:46,966 --> 02:17:47,683
...or...

1527
02:17:49,846 --> 02:17:55,004
...we will rule forever
under the banner of Islam.